"hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:"
7015,"(7015) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah did not recite Qunoot. The entire Sunnah is at dawn, and the Qunut is performed in the Witr prayer every night before bowing. Abu Bakr said: This is what we say."
7016,"(7016) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Harith bin Hisham, On the authority of Ali, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say at the end of his Witrah: O God, I seek refuge in Your satisfaction from Your anger, and I seek refuge in you to recover from your punishment, and I seek refuge in you from you, I cannot count your praise, you are as you praised me. yourself (Tirmidhi 3566. Abu Dawud 1422)"
7017,"(7017) Yazid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Sulayman al-Taymi, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Abu al-Muhazam, on the authority of Abu Hariri, he said: I descended upon him for ten years, but I never saw him reciting his Qunoot."
7018,"(7018) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He did not recite Qunoot at Fajr or during Witr, and when he was asked about Qunoot, he said: We do not know Qunoot except for a long time. Standing and reciting the Qur’an."
7019,"(7019) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: The Witr prayer is only for the people of the Qur’an."
7020,"(7020) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Mus’ar, on the authority of Hammad, who said: If he recites Qunoot before reciting Qunoot, let him prostrate. Your prostration of forgetfulness. It means in the string."
7021,"(7021) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Aswad, on the authority of his father; When Abdullah bin Masoud finished reciting the Qur’an, he would say “Allahu Akbar” and then pray Qunoot."
7022,"(7022) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If you want to perform Qunoot, then say takbir for Qunoot. And say “Allahu Akbar” when you want to bow."
7023,"(7023) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; He used to say “Allahu Akbar” when he recited Qunoot, and “Allahu Akbar” when he had finished."
7024,"(7024) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: When you have finished reciting, say “Allahu Akbar”, then when you have finished So say “Allahu Akbar” and bow."
7025,"(7025) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I heard Al-Hakam, Hammad, and Abu Ishaq saying regarding Qunut Al-Witr: When he finishes, he says “Allahu Akbar” and then recites Qunoot."
7026,"(7026) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Raise your hands for Qunoot."
7027,"(7027) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abiyah, on the authority of Abdullah; He used to raise his hand in the Qunut of the Witr."
7028,"(7028) Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah; He used to raise his hand when reciting the Qunoot in the Witr prayer."
7029,"(7029) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: I entered upon the lions one night while he was sick. So he prayed the Witr prayer with a man leaning against him. He said: So you performed Qunoot, and he prolonged the Qunoot, to the point that I thought he had added to what he was doing."
7030,"(7030) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr; He used to lead us in the Witr prayer as often as he recited a hundred verses."
7031,"(7031) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughiryah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The Qunoot al-Witr prayer is performed as much as: {If The heavens split."
7032,"(7032) Ali bin Musahir told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman; He was asked about Qunoot Omar at dawn? He said: He used to recite Qunoot to the extent that a man recites a hundred verses."
7033,"(7033) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham, he said: There is no Witr except with Qunoot."
7034,"(7034) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, who said: I said to my father: O father, you prayed behind the Prophet, may he pray. May God bless him and grant him peace. He succeeded Abu Bakr, Omar, and Uthman. Have you seen any of them recite Qunoot? He said: O my son, it is a hadith. (Tirmidhi 403. Ahmad 3/472)"
7035,"(7035) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Ghassan Al-Muradi, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun; Omar bin Al-Khattab did not recite the Qunoot at dawn."
7036,"(7036) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Abu Malik, on the authority of his father, he said: I told him: I prayed behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Abu Bakr, Omar, and Othman. Did they perform Qunoot? He said: No, my son. This is a hadith. (Ibn Majah 1241. Tabarani 8179)"
7037,"(7037) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Al-Aswad and Amr bin Maimun prayed after Omar after the dawn prayer, but he did not recite the Qunoot."
7038,"(7038) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Yazid, and Amr bin Auspicious; They prayed after the time of dawn and did not recite Qunoot."
7039,"(7039) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Mis`ar narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Arfajah; Ibn Masoud did not recite Qunoot at dawn."
7040,"(7040) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Qais, that Ibn Masoud did not He recites Qunoot at dawn."
7041,"(7041) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah did not recite Qunoot in his prayer. In the morning"
7042,"(7042) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Sulaim Abi Al-Sha’atha’i Al-Muharbibi, he said: I asked Ibn Omar said about Qunoot at dawn, and he said: What is Qunoot? I said, a man gets up quickly after reciting, so Ibn Omar said: I did not feel."
7043,"(7043) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Waqid, the client of Zayd ibn Khalidah, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, On the authority of Ibn Abbas and Ibn Omar that they did not recite the Qunat during dawn."
7044,"(7044) Ruh bin Ubadah narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria bin Ishaq, he said: Amr bin Dinar narrated to me, that Ibn al-Zubayr prayed. They said it in the morning, but they were not satisfied."
7045,"(7045) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, that Omar was not He recites Qunoot at dawn."
7046,"(7046) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, that Omar ibn Al-Khattab did not recite Qunoot at dawn."
7047,"(7047) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Abd al-A’la, on the authority of Talha, that Abu Bakr did not He recites Qunoot at dawn."
7048,"(7048) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Yazid al-Faqir, who said: I prayed the dawn prayer behind Ibn Umar but did not recite the Qunoot."
7049,"(7049) Hushaym told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Imran bin Al-Harith, he said: I prayed with Ibn Abbas in his house. He performed the Fajr prayer and did not recite Qunoot before or after bowing."
7050,"(7050) Hushaym told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Zayd, he said: Ibn Umar said: I did not witness or know about the morning prayer."
7051,"(7051) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Awn narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that He did not recognize Qunoot at dawn."
7052,"(7052) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hisham al-Dastawai narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, only recited Qunut. May God bless him and grant him peace for a month after bowing. (Bukhari 4089. Muslim 304)"
7053,"(7053) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, only recited Qunut. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him in the morning prayer, after bowing, he supplicates for the Rā’l and Dhākān. (Bukhari 4094, Ahmad 3/116)"
7054,"(7054) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, only recited a month of supplication. On people who killed some of their companions, and they are called the Qaraites. (Bukhari 1002, Muslim 469)"
7055,"(7055) Hushaym told us, he said: Orwah Al-Hamdani told us, he said: Al-Sha’bi told us, he said: When you narrated to Ali in Fajr prayer. The people denied that, he said: He said: We only sought victory against our enemy."
7056,"(7056) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Qais narrated to us, on the authority of Amir al-Janni, that Omar bin al-Khattab did not recite Qunoot. At dawn, Amer said: Qunoot did not occur until the people of Syria came."
7057,"(7057) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Qays narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Abdullah said: If the people took a valley And a path, and Omar took a valley and a path. You took the valley of Omar and its path, and if you were obedient to Omar, you would be obedient to Abdullah."
7058,"(7058) Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Bishr told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, that he did not recite Qunoot in Fajr prayer"
7059,"(7059) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr, on the authority of Fudail, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: You only recited Qunuts. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for days. (Tahawi 244)"
7060,"(7060) Waki’ told us, he said: Mis’ar told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah bin Masoud said: He They knew that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, only recited the month. (Tahawi 243. Tabarani 483)"
7061,"(7061) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, who said: I prayed behind Sa’id bin Jubayr, but he did not You have Qunoot."
7062,"(7062) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Nafi’, who said: I prayed the dawn prayer behind Sa’id bin Jubayr, but he did not say the Qunoot."
7063,"(7063) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of a sheikh, that he prayed behind Uthman but he did not recite the Qunoot."
7064,"(7064) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Taymiyy, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: I prayed behind Ibn Umar but he did not say Qunoot. Before bowing, or after it."
7065,"(7065) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Ismail, who said: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr about Qunoot, He said: When you recite, kneel."
7066,"(7066) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I mentioned Abu Ja`far Qunut, and he said: He came out. Ali is from us, and you did not obey, but you obeyed after he came to you."
7067,"(7067) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah and Suleiman, they said: Ibrahim did not He recited Qunoot in the Fajr prayer while he was an imam."
7068,"(7068) Hussein bin Ali narrated to us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Mansour, who said: Mujahid and Saeed bin Jubayr narrated to me, that Ibn Abbas did not recite Qunoot in the Fajr prayer."
7069,"(7069) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, that he used to not recite Qunoot in the morning prayer."
7070,"(7070) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: Neither Abu Bakr nor Omar uttered Qunoot. Fajr"
7071,"(7071) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’tha’i, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Umar that he did not He does it, meaning qunut at dawn."
7072,"(7072) They narrated?? Waki`, he said: Sufyan and Shu`abi narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of al-Bara’, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He recited Qunoot at dawn and sunset. (Muslim 3060, Ahmad 4/299)"
7073,"(7073) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Fitr narrated to us, on the authority of Ata, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited the Qunoot at dawn. (Ahmad 3/162, Bayhaqi 201)"
7074,"(7074) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of an unnamed sheikh, that Abu Bakr recited Qunoot in Fajr"
7075,"(7075) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Maqil, he said: You recited Qunut at dawn. Two men from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Ali and Abu Musa."
7076,"(7076) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Abu Ja`far al-Razi narrated to us, on the authority of al-Rabi’ ibn Anas, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. You recited the Qunoot at dawn."
7077,"(7077) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abu Raja’, who said: I saw Ibn Abbas holding out his frog in Qunoot. His morning prayer when he was in Basra."
7078,"(7078) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Abu Al-Ashhab Ja’far bin Hayyan and Qurayh bin Khalid narrated to us that they heard it from Abu Raja’. Al-Attaridi said: Ibn Abbas prayed the dawn prayer with the sight and it was Qunut."
7079,"(7079) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra al-Zarraad, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, who said: Perhaps Omar recited Qunoot in the Fajr prayer."
7080,"(7080) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, who said that Qunoot is a past Sunnah."
7081,"(7081) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zubaid bin Al-Harith Al-Yami, who said: I asked Ibn Abi Layla about Qunoot. At dawn, he said: A past Sunnah."
7082,"(7082) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Zaid bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he said: Qunoot at dawn"
7083,"(7083) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muharib, on the authority of Ubaid bin Al-Bara’, on the authority of Al-Bara’, that he had Qunoot At dawn"
7084,"(7084) I heard someone saying: I heard Sufyan saying: Whoever performs Qunoot is good, and whoever does not perform Qunoot is good, and whoever performs Qunoot is only Qunoot. upon the imam, and there is no Qunoot upon those behind him."
7085,"(7085) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Al-Awwam bin Hamza, he said: I asked Abu Uthman about Qunoot, and he said: After Bowing, so I said: From whom? He said: On the authority of Abu Bakr, Omar, and Othman."
7086,"(7086) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abu Raja’, who said: I prayed with Ibn Abbas in the Basra Mosque. You performed the morning prayer with us before bowing."
7087,"(7087) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Awf. He said: I mentioned that to Abu Al-Minhal, so he narrated to me, on the authority of my father. Al-Aaliyah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in a similar manner."
7088,"(7088) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, who said: The Prophet’s prayers and prayers were Qunut. May God bless him and grant him peace for forty mornings in the morning prayer after bowing."
7089,"(7089) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ayyash Al-Amiri, on the authority of Ibn Maqil, that Omar, Ali, and Abu Musa recited Qunoot At dawn, before bowing."
7090,"(7090) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abu al-Jahm, on the authority of al-Bara’, that he had recited Qunoot before The rak'ah"
7091,"(7091) Hushaym told us, he said: Yazid bin Abi Ziyad told us, he said: Zayd bin Wahhab told us, that Omar bin Al-Khattab recited Qunoot in the morning prayer before bowing."
7092,"(7092) Hushaym told us, he said: Ali bin Zaid told us, he said: Abu Uthman al-Nahdi told us, he said, I prayed behind Omar Ibn Al-Khattab performed the Fajr prayer and performed Qunoot before bowing."
7093,"(7093) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib narrated to us, on the authority of Abi Abd al-Rahman al-Salami, that Ali was He recites Qunoot in the morning prayer before bowing."
7094,"(7094) Hushaym told us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, he said: I prayed After Umar al-Fughda, he said, “You performed the Qunut in it before bowing.”"
7095,"(7095) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Omar, in the same way."
7096,"(7096) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Nasir ibn Dhu’luq, he said: I prayed behind Rabi’ ibn Khathim and I performed Qunoot. Before the rak'ah."
7097,"(7097) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Qays, who said: I prayed behind Ubaydah at dawn and performed Qunoun before The rak'ah"
7098,"(7098) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Abu Farwa, who said: Ibn Abi Layla used to recite Qunoot at dawn Before the rak'ah."
7099,"(7099) Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Wahhab, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: He used to make many supplications. In the morning prayer before bowing."
7100,"(7100) Hushaym told us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, he said: I prayed Omar ibn al-Khattab came after lunch, and said in his supplication: O God, we seek Your help and seek Your forgiveness, and we praise You with goodness, and no We disbelieve in you, and we disavow, and we leave behind whoever denounces you. Oh God, we worship you, and to you we pray and prostrate, and to you we seek and descend, we hope. Your mercy and we fear Your punishment. Indeed, Your punishment is attached to the disbelievers."
7101,"(7101) Hushaym told us, saying: Husayn told us, on the authority of Zurr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of His father, he prayed behind Omar, so he did the same."
7102,"(7102) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Suwayd. Al-Kailili said that Ali recited these two surahs at dawn: O God, we seek Your help and seek Your forgiveness and praise You. And we do not disbelieve in you, and we renounce and abandon those who disbelieve in you. O God, we worship you, and to you we pray and prostrate, and to you we seek and conceive. We hope for Your mercy, and we fear Your punishment. Indeed, Your punishment is attached to the disbelievers. (Bayhaqi 204. Ibn Saad 241)"
7103,"(7103) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ja`far ibn Burqan informed us, on the authority of Maimun ibn Mihran, regarding the readings of Ubayy ibn Ka`b: Oh God, we seek Your help, we seek Your forgiveness, and we praise You, but we do not disbelieve in You, and we shun and leave behind whoever denounces You, O God, beware of you. We worship, but to You we pray and prostrate, and to You we seek and rejoice. We hope for Your mercy and fear Your punishment. Indeed, Your punishment is attached to the disbelievers."
7104,"(7104) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, who said: I heard Umar say Qunoot. At dawn he says: In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.
 Oh God, we seek your help, we believe in you, we trust in you, we praise you for goodness, and we do not disbelieve in you.
 Then he recited: In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. And we fear Your punishment. Indeed, Your severe punishment is upon the disbelievers. Oh God, punish the disbelief of the People of the Book who turn away from Spielke"
7105,"(7105) Hushaym told us, he said: Husayn told us, he said: I prayed the morning prayer one day and Uthman bin Ziyad, he said: So I performed the Qunoot in the morning prayer, he said: And when I finished my prayer, he said to me what you said in your Qunoot, he said: So I said, I mentioned These words, O God, we seek Your help and seek Your forgiveness and praise You for goodness, and we do not disbelieve in You and remove and forsake those who Fajruk, O God, to You we worship, and to You we pray and prostrate, and to You we seek and descend. We hope for Your mercy and fear Your severe torment. Your punishment is due to the disbelievers. Othman said: This is what Omar bin Al-Khattab and Othman bin Affan used to do."
7106,"(7106) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mukhariq, on the authority of Tariq ibn Shihab, that he prayed behind Umar ibn The dawn speaker, and when he finished reciting the recitation, he said the takbir, then he recited Qunoot, then he said the takbir, then he bowed."
7107,"(7107) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-A`la, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Salami, that Ali said the greatest When he recited the Qunoot at dawn and he said “Allahu Akbar” when he bowed."
7108,"(7108) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abu al-Jahm, who said: Al-Bara’ used to say “Allahu Akbar” before he said Qunoot."
7109,"(7109) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abu al-Jahm, on the authority of al-Bara’, that he recited Qunoot at dawn He said “Allahu Akbar” when he finished reciting the Qur’an, and “Allahu Akbar” when he bowed."
7110,"(7110) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Mahan, who said: He used to say takbir before he You recite Qunoot in the Fajr prayer."
7111,"(7111) Humaid bin Abdul-Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Abu Abdul-Rahman, that it was He says “Allahu Akbar” before saying Qunoot in the Fajr prayer and when he wants to bow."
7112,"(7112) Humayd narrated to us on the authority of Zuhayr, he said: I said to Abu Ishaq: “You should say takbir before you recite Qunoun in the Fajr prayer.” He said: Yes"
7113,"(7113) Nasr bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, that it was Qunoot opens with the takbeer."
7114,"(7114) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Maymun, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: Omar used to say Qunoot to us after He bows and raises his hands until he appears to be a hyena and his voice can be heard from behind the mosque."
7115,"(7115) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ja’far, the author of Al-Anmatat, on the authority of Abu Uthman, that Omar raised his hand in Qunoot. Fajr"
7116,"(7116) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Khallas bin Amr Al-Hijri, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that He prayed and you followed them at dawn in Basra, and he raised his hand until he stretched out a hyena."
7117,"(7117) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abu Raja’, who said: I saw Ibn Abbas holding his frog in Qunoot. Lunch prayer"
7118,"(7118) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abu Farwa, who said: Ibn Abi Layla used to pray With one finger, he says in the Qunoot of Fajr."
7119,"(7119) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, raised He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, bowed his head from the morning prayer. He said, “O God, save Al-Walid bin Al-Walid and save him bin Hisham and Ayyash bin Abi.” My people and those who are oppressed in Mecca. O God, intensify Your power over Mudar and make it upon them for years like the years of Joseph. (Bukhari 6200 and Muslim 294)"
7120,"(7120) Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Ibn Yahnas, on the authority of Saeed bin Zaid, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited his prayers, and he said: O God, curse the sheep and the male and the muscle, and disobeying you disobeys God. And His Messenger."
7121,"(7121) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-A’la, that Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Salami recited the Qunoot at dawn He calls on Qatari."
7122,"(7122) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr ibn Qays, on the authority of someone who heard Abraham say, “Men are not named during prayer.”"
7123,"(7123) Hushaym told us, he said: Husayn told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Maqil told us, he said: I prayed with Ali. During his lunch prayer, he said: You recited the Qunoot, and he said in his Qunoot: O God, bless you with your companions, your companions, and Amr bin Al-Aas. And his followers, Abu Al-Awar Al-Salami, Abdullah bin Qais and his followers."
7124,"(7124) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban told us, he said he stayed For forty mornings, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited Qunoot in the morning prayer after bowing, and he used to say in his Qunot: O God. Save Al-Walid bin Al-Walid, Ayyash bin Abi Rabi’ah, Al-Aas bin Hisham, and the oppressed among the believers in Mecca who They cannot evade it, nor do they find a way."
7125,"(7125) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, on the authority of Imran ibn Abi Anas, on the authority of Hanzala ibn Ali Al-Aslami, on the authority of Khafaf bin Ima bin Rahdha Al-Ghafari, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led us in prayer at dawn. When he raised his head from the last rak’ah, he said: May God curse Lahyan, Ra’l, and Dhakwan, and your disobedience disobeyed God and His Messenger, Aslam. May God bless her, forgiving, may God forgive her. Then he fell down, prostrating, and when he finished the prayer, he turned to the people facing him, and said: Oh, the people. It was not I who said this, but God said it. (Muslim 307. Ahmad 57)"
7126,"(7126) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If he forgets to recite Qunoot at dawn, then he must perform two prostrations of forgetfulness."
7127,"(7127) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, who said: He was asked about a man who made a mistake and did Qunoot, and he said: This one made a mistake and did it correctly."
7128,"(7128) Al-Walid bin Uqba narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, he said: Whoever saw Qunoot did not Qunoot, on it you prostrated the forgetfulness."
7129,"(7129) Abdullah bin Idris, Waki’ and Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bai, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed Qunoot in the morning and sunset times. He said: So he said: Ibrahim was like the companions of Abdullah, but he was the companion of princes, and no one mentioned anyone saying Abraham (Tirmidhi 401, Abu Dawud 1436)"
7130,"(7130) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Maqil, who said: I prayed Maghrib behind Ali, and I performed Qunoot."
7131,"(7131) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalabab, on the authority of Anas, he said two prayers in which he recited the Maghrib prayer. And dawn."
7132,"(7132) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Khalid, on the authority of Ibn Maqil, he said, “Ali recited Qunut.” Morocco"
7133,"(7133) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit Al-Thumali, who said: I asked Abu Ja`far about Qunoot, and he said: Every prayer is recited with Qunoot. In it, in it is Qunoot."
7134,"(7134) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, who said: Abdullah saw a man He prays with his feet straight, and he said: If he had kept this between his feet, it would have been better."
7135,"(7135) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Misra al-Nahdi, on the authority of al-Manhal, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: He came out Abdullah went from his house to the mosque, and saw a man praying with his feet straight. Abdullah said, “This man has made a mistake.” The Sunnah, even if it were separated from one another, it would be more beloved to me. (Nasa’i 967)"
7136,"(7136) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Uyaynah ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: I was with my father in the mosque and he saw a pure man. Between his feet, he said: Stick one of them to the other. In this mosque, I saw eighteen of the Prophet’s companions. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. I have never seen any of them do this."
7137,"(7137) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: I saw Amr ibn Maymun moving between his feet during prayer."
7138,"(7138) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, who said: I saw Amr bin Maimun moving between his feet, placing This is for this and this is for this."
7139,"(7139) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Yusuf bin Abd, who said: I saw Ibn Sirin praying while he was Thus, it means putting one leg in front and the other behind."
7140,"(7140) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, who said: Ibn Sirin used to move his feet while praying."
7141,"(7141) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rashid, who said: I saw an alcoholic man leaning on his feet. This is one time, and this is another time in prayer."
7142,"(7142) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Abi Bakr, who said: I saw a man who did not line up his feet during prayer. And he moves it while he prays."
7143,"(7143) Abd al-Zubayr told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of a man, that Ibn al-Zubayr used to line up between His feet in prayer."
7144,"(7144) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, who said: Tell me who saw Ibn al-Zubayr praying, lined up between His feet and attached one to the other."
7145,"(7145) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Husayn, who said: I saw Ibn Maqil praying with his feet straight."
7146,"(7146) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I saw Muslim bin Yassar praying as if he was an unwavering friend. A bitter man, and a bitter man against me."
7147,"(7147) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, who said: I saw Ibn Umar praying standing in a row. Its ancients, as far as we know."
7148,"(7148) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Ismail ibn Muslim, on the authority of Malik ibn Dinar, who said: I saw Ikrimah praying Clear between his feet."
7149,"(7149) Zayd bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Quraysh bin Hayyan, who said: I saw Al-Hasan praying with his feet straight."
7150,"(7150) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Mukhtar bin Saad, who said: I saw Al-Qasim bin Muhammad lining his feet in prayer. And there is no separation between them."
7151,"(7151) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Whoever enters the mosque and has already prayed, he said: It begins with the written word."
7152,"(7152) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah. And Hafs, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, said: It begins with what is written."
7153,"(7153) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: He begins with what is written."
7154,"(7154) Hushaym and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, who said, “Begin with what you came for.”"
7155,"(7155) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: Start with what is written."
7156,"(7156) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said, “Start with what is written.”"
7157,"(7157) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aflah, he said: I and the one who divided the mosque came and they had prayed, so he prayed for himself, meaning he began. In writing"
7158,"(7158) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: They used to begin with what was written."
7159,"(7159) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, he said: Al-Hakam said: They used to begin with the obligatory prayer. Abu Ishaq said: They used to start with the obligatory prayer."
7160,"(7160) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Dhurayh, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The example of one who enters a mosque. He prayed therein, so he performed voluntary prayers, like one who performs Umrah before performing Hajj."
7161,"(7161) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Laila, He said, “Begin with what you came for.”"
7162,"(7162) Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Dhurayh, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, about a man who entered a mosque and had prayed. Should his family volunteer? He said, “It is like a man who volunteers before he performs Hajj.”"
7163,"(7163) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mansour, and Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan that he did not see any harm in volunteering."
7164,"(7164) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Zirr, who said, “He may volunteer if he wishes.”"
7165,"(7165) Hushaym told us, on the authority of the common people, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Dhail, that he used to volunteer if he preceded In writing"
7166,"(7166) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: Al-Hasan was asked about a man entering the mosque while its people had prayed, he said: He said: : As for me, I was praying as I was praying before that."
7167,"(7167) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Hammad, who said: There is no harm in it if it is during the time of prayer."
7168,"(7168) Waki’ told us, he said: Shuabi told us, he said: Hammad said: He may volunteer if he wants."
7169,"(7169) Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus bin Ubaid told us, he said: Abu Uthman Al-Yashkuri told me, he said: He passed. Anas bin Malik was among us, and we had prayed the morning prayer, and with him was a group. He commanded a man from among them and he gave the call to prayer, then they prayed two rak’ahs. Before dawn. He said, then he ordered him to stand, then he went forward and led them in prayer."
7170,"(7170) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Al-Ja’d Abu Uthman, on the authority of Anas, similar to this."
7171,"(7171) Muadh bin Muadh told us, on the authority of Abu Hurr, he said: I and Abdullah bin Hamid entered a mosque and he prayed in it, and he said “Won’t you come until we pray in congregation?” I said: “Some of them disliked that.” He said: “My father saw no harm in that.”"
7172,"(7172) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Naji, on the authority of Abu al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Abu Saeed, he said: A man came while the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had prayed, and he said: Which of you would trade in this? He said, so he stood up. A man from the people prayed with him. (Tirmidhi 220, Ahmad 3/64)"
7173,"(7173) Hushaym told us, he said: Sulayman al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Abu Uthman, he said: A man entered the mosque and he had prayed. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Isn’t there a man who gives this in charity and gets up and prays with him?"
7174,"(7174) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zayd, who said: I entered a warrior’s mosque with Abraham, and they had prayed and he was secure."
7175,"(7175) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ziyad, a client of Quraysh, who said: I entered the Basra Mosque with Al-Hasan and found them there. Pray and pray with me."
7176,"(7176) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he did not think there was anything wrong with praying in congregation after the congregational prayer. Al-Kala’ Mosque in Basra."
7177,"(7177) Hushaym told us, he said: Mansour told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: They only hated to gather people who feared Sultan"
7178,"(7178) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Musafer al-Jassas, on the authority of Fudayl ibn Amr, that Adiy ibn Thabit and his companions returned from A funeral, so they entered a mosque in which prayers had been prayed, and they gathered together the thoughts of Abraham."
7179,"(7179) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abd Rabbuh ibn Abi Rashid, he said: Al-Hayy told us, he said: Anas ibn Malik came to us and he We prayed the morning prayer and he led the prayer, then he led them in prayer and he stood among them."
7180,"(7180) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Ata’, that he and Ibn Atiy prayed and greeted him in The Sacred Mosque in congregation after its people had prayed."
7181,"(7181) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, that he said: They all pray in one row with their imam in front of them. Among them"
7182,"(7182) Ishaq Al-Azraq narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Salma ibn Kuhayl, that Ibn Masoud He entered the mosque and they had prayed, so he gathered Baalqamah, Masruq, and Al-Aswad."
7183,"(7183) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say: They pray individually."
7184,"(7184) Hushaym told us, saying: Khaled told us, on the authority of Abu Qalab, that he used to say: They pray individually."
7185,"(7185) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: They pray individually."
7186,"(7186) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: They pray in winter."
7187,"(7187) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawi, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They pray individually."
7188,"(7188) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of Kathir, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace When they enter the mosque and he has prayed there, they pray individually."
7189,"(7189) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aflah, he said: We entered the mosque with Al-Qasim and he had prayed in it. He said: So Al-Qasim prayed. Alone"
7190,"(7190) Hushaym told us, he said: Mansour told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ali, that he used to say: Who will catch you with The imam said two rak'ahs. He said: He recites what he has overtaken."
7191,"(7191) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Rabi’ bin Abi Abd al-Rahman, that Omar bin al-Khattab and Aba al-Darda’ were They say: Whatever you catch of the imam’s prayer, make it the first of your prayer."
7192,"(7192) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Amr bin Muhajir, who said: I heard Omar bin Abdul Aziz say: Make him first. Your prayers"
7193,"(7193) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id and Al-Hasan, who said: Whatever you catch with the Imam, he is the first. Your prayers"
7194,"(7194) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ali, similar to him."
7195,"(7195) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: Sa’id bin Jubayr used to say: He recites whatever he perceives because it He used to facilitate the recitation behind the imam."
7196,"(7196) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali; Concerning a man who misses a rak’ah or two rak’ahs with the imam, he said: He recites while the imam is silent. Al-Hasan said the same thing."
7197,"(7197) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: What did you realize with the Imam? It is your last prayer."
7198,"(7198) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: Make another Your prayer is the first of your prayers."
7199,"(7199) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to make what he achieved with the imam last. His prayers"
7200,"(7200) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that when he gathered with the imam, he did not recite. So when he stands up, he recites."
7201,"(7201) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he said: Recite what you decide."
7202,"(7202) Hushaym told us, he said: Husayn and Mughiry told us, on the authority of Abraham, he said: It is recited in what is decided."
7203,"(7203) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I asked Mujahid about a man who missed two rak’ahs with the imam and he recited during them. He said: Make your last prayer your first prayer."
7204,"(7204) Abdul-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, about a man who missed some of the prayers, so he got up and made up for it. He said: : He makes what remains the beginning of his prayer, and if you know what the imam has recited, then recite it."
7205,"(7205) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Omar, who said: I heard Amr bin Dinar say: Make up what you missed as you missed it."
7206,"(7206) Ya’qub bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, and Ibn Sirin, that they said: Among those who came before him Imam: If you finish the prayer after him, complete your recitation."
7207,"(7207) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, who said: Ubaid bin Umair went to Raka’i from Morocco, and I heard him reciting. And when the night covers you."
7208,"(7208) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, he said: Ibrahim Al-Nakha’i used to recite what he decided."
7209,"(7209) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is disliked for one of his legs to be raised above the other. During prayer, or leaning against a wall except on top."
7210,"(7210) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yahya bin Hani’, who said: I saw Amr bin Maymun standing and praying. He placed one of his legs on top of the other."
7211,"(7211) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: I heard Anas say: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, fell. On the authority of a mare whose right flank broke open, so we entered upon him to return to him, and the time for prayer came and he led us in prayer sitting, so we prayed behind him sitting, so when He finished the prayer and said: The imam was appointed only to be followed in prayer. So when he says “Allahu Akbar,” they should pronounce “Allahu Akbar,” and when he bowed, “so they should bow,” and when he said, “Allah hears.” To whomever praises Him, say, “Our Lord, to You is all praise.” And when he prays sitting, pray sitting all together. (Bukhari 1114, Muslim 77)"
7212,"(7212) Abdou told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, complained. He said the salutation, and some of his companions entered to visit him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed sitting, and they prayed standing with his prayer. So he motioned to them to sit down, so they sat down, and when he left, he said: The imam has only been appointed to be followed, so when he bows, bow down, and when he rises So rise up, and if he prays sitting, pray sitting. (Bukhari 688 and Abu Dawud 605)"
7213,"(7213) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was struck by epilepsy. On the authority of his horse, it fell on the trunk of a palm tree and its foot broke off, so we went in to visit him while he was praying in a drinking place. Aisha was sitting and we prayed with his prayer while we were standing, then we entered upon him another time while he was praying sitting and we prayed. With his prayer while we were standing, he motioned to us to sit down, and when he prayed, he said: The imam was only appointed to be followed, so when he prayed, he was standing. So pray standing, and if he prays sitting, pray sitting, and do not stand while he is sitting as the people of Persia do with their great lords. (Abu Dawud 602. Ahmad 3/334)"
7214,"(7214) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hariri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The imam has only been appointed to be followed in prayer, so when he says “Allahu Akbar”, they should say “Allahu Akbar”, and when He recited, so listen, and when he said, “It is not the One upon whom Anger is angry, nor those who have gone astray, then say ‘Ameen,’” and when he bowed, then kneel, and when he said, “He heard.” God belongs to those who praise Him, so say, “O God, our Lord, to You is praise.” And when he prostrates, then prostrate, and if he prays sitting, then pray sitting."
7215,"(7215) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa`id, who said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that Jabir He complained to them about Mecca, so when he returned, he went out, and they went out with him, following him until when they reached a certain distance, Hazrat One of the prayers, so he prayed with them sitting, and they prayed with him sitting."
7216,"(7216) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Imam is an emir, so if he prays standing So they pray standing, and if he prays sitting, then they pray sitting."
7217,"(7217) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qais bin Qad, who said: Our imam complained, so he prayed sitting for several days. So we prayed with his prayer, and he said: Abu Hurairah is the Imam Amir, so if he prays standing, then they pray standing, and if he prays sitting, then they pray sitting."
7218,"(7218) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hubaira, that Usaid bin Hudayr was leading his people, Banu Abd al-Ashhal, and he complained, so he went out to them after he complained, and they said to him: He came forward and said: I cannot pray. They said: No one will lead us except you as long as you remain. So he said: Sit down and he prayed with them sitting down."
7219,"(7219) Khaled bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, who said: I heard Al-Qasim bin Muhammad say, Mu'awiyah said, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If the imam prays sitting, pray sitting. He said, so the people were amazed at his sincerity. Muawiyah"
7220,"(7220) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Qais bin Qaid, he said: It was ours. An imam fell ill, so we prayed him while sitting."
7221,"(7221) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, he said: Abdullah said, “The imam was only appointed to be followed.” So when he says takbeer, say takbeer, and when he bows, then bow, and when he prostrates, prostrate, for he is the first to rise and the first to lower."
7222,"(7222) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Talha, who said: Salman said: Whoever raises his head before the imam and lowers His head is before the imam, so his forelock is in the hand of Satan, and he raises it and lowers it."
7223,"(7223) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Malih bin Abdullah Al-Saadi, who said: Abu Hurairah said: He who lowers and raises his head before the imam, his forelock is in the hand of Satan."
7224,"(7224) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Is not the one who raises his head before the imam afraid that God will turn his head into the head of a donkey? (Bukhari 691, Abu Dawud 623)"
7225,"(7225) Wakā’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ziyad bin Fayyad, on the authority of Tamim bin Salamah, who said: Abdullah said: As for The one who raises his head before the imam fears that God will turn his head into the head of a dog."
7226,"(7226) Hushaym told us, he said: The common people told us, on the authority of Ezra bin Al-Harith, that he told him, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib He said: When we prayed behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and raised our heads from bowing, we would stand in rows until he prostrated. So when he prostrated, We followed him. (Ahmad 4/292, Abu Ali 1673)"
7227,"(7227) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: I have come, so do not hasten to kneel or prostrate, for I will precede you in doing so. When I kneel, you will overtake me with it when I am raised, and as I precede you with it, when I prostrate, you will overtake me with it when I am lowered."
7228,"(7228) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban, on the authority of Ibn Muhayriz, on the authority of Mu'awiyah, he raised him like him. (Abu Dawud 619; Ahmed 98)"
7229,"(7229) Hushaym and Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal ibn Yasaf, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, who said: He said: Abdullah: Do not hasten with your imams in bowing or prostrating."
7230,"(7230) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, who said: Who He was with the imam, so he bowed before he bowed and prostrated before he prostrated, so he is not with him."
7231,"(7231) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Khams, who said: I prayed next to Abu Qalabi, and he did not do anything even It was made by the Imam."
7232,"(7232) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib, He said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, raised his head from bowing, none of us would bend his back until he had prostrated. So when he prostrated, We followed him. (Bukhari 747. Abu Dawud 620)"
7233,"(7233) Ali bin Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mukhtar bin Falfil, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led us in prayer. One day he gave the salutation, and when he had finished the prayer, he turned to face us and said: O people, I am your imam, so do not precede me. By bowing, nor by prostration, nor by standing, nor by leaving, for I see you in front of me and behind me. (Muslim 112. Abu Dawud 624)"
7234,"(7234) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Muhammad hated to precede the imam with some form of takbeer."
7235,"(7235) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ibn Abi Aroub told us, he said: His leaders told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Jubayr, on the authority of Hattan bin Abdullah said: Abu Musa led us in prayer, and when he turned, he said: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed us and explained it clearly. We have our Sunnah and taught us our prayer. He said: When the Imam says “Allahu Akbar,” “Allahu Akbar,” and when he bows, bow, for the Imam bows before you and raises his voice. Before you (Muslim 303. Abu Dawud 965)"
7236,"(7236) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Qays narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Mudarik, that when Mu’adh came to Yemen, he was He taught Nakha’, so he said to them: If you see me doing something during prayer, do the same. When he prostrated, Ghosn hurt his eyes. A tree and he broke it in prayer, so each man among them went to a branch in prayer and broke it, and when he prayed, he said, “I only broke it.” Because it hurt my eyes when I prostrated, and you did well in what you obeyed."
7237,"(7237) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr bin Mutim, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: I am a man who has come, so do not hasten to stand up or prostrate. (Ibn Saad 420, Tabarani 1579)"
7238,"(7238) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: When the Messenger of God fell ill May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. During his illness during which he died, Bilal came to call him to prayer, and he said: Tell Abu Bakr so that he may lead the people in prayer. We said, O Messenger of God, that Abu Bakr is a gentle and wretched man, and when he takes your place he cries, but he is not able to do so. If you command Omar, He said: Order Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer, for you are Joseph’s companions. So he sent for Abu Bakr and he led the people in prayer, and he found the Prophet. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, he put on his sandals and went out to pray, guided between two men, his feet stepping on the ground. When Abu Bakr sensed this, he went to stay behind, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, motioned to him to take your place. She said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and sat next to Abu Bakr, and Abu Bakr was following the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, and the people trust Abu Bakr. (Muslim 951, Ibn Majah 1232)"
7239,"(7239) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Sufyan bin Hussein told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, he said: When he fell ill The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during his illness in which he died, Bilal came to him and called him to prayer, and said: O Bilal, I conveyed the message, so whoever wants, let him pray, and whoever wants, let him leave. So he said: O Messenger of God, who will lead the people in prayer? He said: Order Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. When Abu Bakr came forward, the curtains were lifted from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. We looked at it as if it were a white piece of paper with a quilt on it, so Abu Bakr thought that he wanted to leave, so he was late. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, advised him to pray where you are, so Abu Bakr prayed, and we did not see the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May peace and blessings be upon him until he died from that day. (Bukhari 680 and Muslim 98)"
7240,"(7240) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Abu Musa said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fell ill and his illness became severe, so he said: Tell Abu Bakr so that he may lead the people in prayer. She said: Aisha, O Messenger of God, that Abu Bakr is a delicate man, and when he takes your place, he is not able to lead the people in prayer, so he said: “Perhaps.” Abu Bakr, let him lead the people in prayer, for you are the companions of Joseph. He said: So Abu Bakr led them in prayer. He greeted the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. (Bukhari 678 and Muslim 101)"
7241,"(7241) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God’s peace and blessings be upon them, and Abu Bakr was behind him, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said “Allahu Akbar” and so Abu Bakr said “Allahu Akbar.” People listen. (Muslim 85. Abu Dawud 606)"
7242,"(7242) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayed, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: When the Prophet died, he prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace. The Ansar said, “Among us is a leader and there is a leader among you.” So Umar came to them and said: O people of the Ansar, do you not know? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. They said: Yes, he said: Which of you is good? He wanted Abu Bakr to advance. (Nasa’i 852. Ahmad 1/396)"
7243,"(7243) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu Salamah bin Abd al-Rahman narrating, The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, complained and said: Tell Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, found He lowered his socks off and went out. When Abu Bakr saw him, he went to stay behind, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, motioned to him. And he greeted you in your place. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came and sat next to Abu Bakr. Abu Bakr was completing By the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the people trust Abu Bakr."
7244,"(7244) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Asim bin Abi Al-Najjoud, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, She said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, fainted, and when he woke up, he said: Did the people pray? She said: So we said: No. He said: Tell Abu Bakr so that he may lead the people in prayer. She said: So we said: O Messenger of God, may God bless you and grant him peace, that Abu Bakr is a miserable man. He said: Asif is the gentle, the most merciful. And when he takes your place, he will not be able to lead the people in prayer. She said: Then he fainted, then he woke up, and he said: Like that. She responded to him three times, and he said: Indeed, the companions of Joseph passed away. Let Abu Bakr lead the people in prayer. She said: Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, found some sandals on himself, so he went out among the wilderness. And he was a Nubian, his sandals were streaked with the white of the soles of his feet, and Abu Bakr was leading the people, so when Abu Bakr saw him, he went He was late, so he motioned to him not to be late. She said: So Abu Bakr stood next to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sitting. Abu Bakr prayed with the prayer of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, while the people prayed with his prayer. Abu Bakr (Ibn Hibban 2118)"
7245,"(7245) Shababah ibn Siwar narrated to us, saying: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Nu’aym ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed during his illness in which he died succeeding Abu Bakr. sitting (Tirmidhi 362. Ahmad 6/159)"
7246,"(7246) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah bin Utba, he said: I came to Aisha and said: Why don’t you tell me about the illness of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: Yes. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became heavy and said: Did the people pray? So I said, “No, they are waiting for you, O Messenger of God.” He said, “Put some water in the basin for me.” She said, “So we did so, so he took a bath, then he went.” He fainted and fainted, then he woke up and said: Did the people pray? So we said, “No, they are waiting for you.” He said: “Put some water in the basin for me.” She said: “So we did so, so he took a bath, then he went to sleep.” So he fainted, then he woke up and said: Did the people pray? So we said: They are waiting for you, O Messenger of God, while the people were sitting in the mosque waiting for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. For the last evening prayer. 
 She said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent to Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. The Messenger came to him and said: Indeed, the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He commanded you to lead the people in prayer. He said: Abu Bakr, who was a gentle man. O Umar, lead the people. So he said to him: Omar, you have more right to that. So Abu Bakr led them in prayer in those days.
 She said, “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, found himself slippers, so he went out between two men for the noon prayer. And Abu Bakr was leading the people in prayer, she said. When Abu Bakr saw him, he went to stay behind, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, motioned to him. He, peace and blessings be upon him, told them not to be late, and he said to them: Sit me next to him, so they made him sit next to Abu Bakr, so Abu Bakr prays while he is standing with the prayer of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the people pray with the prayer of Abu Bakr and the Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace, sitting.
 Ubaid Allah said: So I entered upon Abdullah bin Abbas and said: Shall I not show you what Aisha told me about the illness of the Messenger of God? God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Come.” So I presented her hadith to him, but he did not deny any of it. (Bukhari 6650, Muslim 311)"
7247,"(7247) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Amr ibn Wahhab, on the authority of Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’ba, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed behind Abdul Rahman bin Awf. (Muslim 81. Ahmad 248)"
7248,"(7248) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl ibn Saad, who said: There was a man among the Ansar, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to him. May God bless him and grant him peace, so that he might reconcile between them. He said: Then he came while Abu Bakr was leading the people in prayer. He said: So he prayed behind Abu Bakr. (Bukhari 1201, Abu Dawud 938)"
7249,"(7249) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He saw no harm in a man removing his robe. On his knees while praying."
7250,"(7250) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he disliked it."
7251,"(7251) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm if a man sits during prayer. He puts his cloak around his shoulders."
7252,"(7252) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade And peace be upon him, about sleeping before it, meaning dinner."
7253,"(7253) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Sayyar ibn Salamah, on the authority of Abu Barza, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was May God bless him and grant him peace. He forbids sleeping before the evening prayer."
7254,"(7254) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Mujahid, who said: Ibn Umar almost cursed the one who He sleeps, missing dinner."
7255,"(7255) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of his father, he said: I was informed on the authority of Anas, he said: We used to avoid beds before prayer. Dinner"
7256,"(7256) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Aslam, who said: Amrula wrote that he slept before he prayed it. Whoever sleeps, his eyes have not slept."
7257,"(7257) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Safiyya, on the authority of Omar, in a similar vein to the hadith of Al-Thaqafiyyah."
7258,"(7258) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Sa’id bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: A man came to him. He said: Among us are those who farm and farm, so is there anything wrong with us if we sleep before the evening prayer? He said: Yes, a hardship, a hardship, and three hardships."
7259,"(7259) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Haytham Al-Muradi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that a man asked him about that, and he said: : Pray, then sleep. He said, then he told him that three times, and on the third time he said: Pray, then sleep, so your eyes did not sleep."
7260,"(7260) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Mujahid, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Whoever sleeps on her side, his eye will not sleep on her, meaning the evening prayer."
7261,"(7261) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I do not like Sleeping before it, nor talking after it."
7262,"(7262) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid that they were They hate sleeping before it and talking after it."
7263,"(7263) Waki’ and Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, who said: I asked the poor Yazid, did I hear Ibn Umar hate sleeping? He accepted it, he said yes."
7264,"(7264) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They hated sleeping before her. And the hadith after it."
7265,"(7265) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Talhah, on the authority of Ata’, in the Almighty’s saying: (Their sides shall distance themselves from their beds.) He said: On the authority of darkness."
7266,"(7266) Shuabi told us, on the authority of Sahl Al-Qurashi, who said: I heard Saeed bin Al-Musayyab saying: Because I pray the evening prayer in... This hour, and that after sunset, is more beloved to me than sleeping during it, then getting up and praying it."
7267,"(7267) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abdul-Malik narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Karim Abi Umayyah, on the authority of Mujahid said: Because I pray the Isha’a prayer before twilight sets is more beloved to me than to sleep during it and then pray it after that. Compassion is absent in a group."
7268,"(7268) Hafs, Ibn Fudail and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah al-Razi, on the authority of His grandmother, and it was a secret to Ali, that Ali might have fallen asleep before dinner."
7269,"(7269) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Husayn, that Khabbab fell asleep and missed dinner."
7270,"(7270) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Husayn, that Abu Wa’il and Abdullah’s companions were sleeping before Dinner"
7271,"(7271) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The black man would not break his fast in Ramadan until he had prayed. So he used to sleep between Maghrib and Isha."
7272,"(7272) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: I told him: Was Ibn Umar sleeping on her behalf, meaning Evening, he said: He used to sleep and appointed someone to wake him up."
7273,"(7273) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, that he used to sleep before her."
7274,"(7274) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ali al-Azdi, who said: He used to conclude He recited the Qur’an every night in Ramadan, and he used to sleep between Maghrib and Isha’."
7275,"(7275) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: They used to sleep like you do before prayer."
7276,"(7276) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Waqa’i, that Sa’id bin Jubayr used to sleep before he prayed. Isha, then he performs Ramadan."
7277,"(7277) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, that he used to sleep before dinner."
7278,"(7278) Ismail bin Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: I was informed that Abu Musa al-Ash’ari repeated He prayed the morning prayer three times that day, then he sat, until it became clear to him that he had prayed at night, then he repeated it, then He prayed and sat until it became clear that he had prayed at night, then he repeated it the third time."
7279,"(7279) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, that Ibn Umar repeated the morning prayer, combining it three times in the day. So, if he had prayed at night, then he repeated it the third time."
7280,"(7280) Hushaym told us, he said: Mansour told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: They doubted the coming of dawn during the reign of Ibn Abbas. He said: So he ordered the muezzin to establish the prayer, then he went forward and led them in prayer and called for the cows until he concluded them, then he bowed, then prostrated. Then he got up and asked the family of Imran to open the door until they sealed it, then he bowed down and prostrated, saying, “And the morning light was lit for them.”"
7281,"(7281) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Husayn narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I had a cough that came out? I came out for the morning prayer. So the muezzin heard your coughing and thought it was dawn, so he established the prayer and we prayed. Then we looked and saw that dawn had not come, so we prepared. Prayer"
7282,"(7282) Hatem bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Othman Al-Makhzoumi, who said: My grandmother told me, on the authority of a servant of Abd. Al-Rahman bin Awf, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, who said: I heard him say: If a menstruating woman purifies herself before sunset, she should pray the noon prayer. And the afternoon prayer, and if she purifies herself before dawn, she performs the sunset and evening prayers."
7283,"(7283) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah and Ubaidah told him, on the authority of Abraham, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’. Al-Sha’bi, and on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of a woman who is menstruating, if she purifies herself before sunset, she prays the noon and afternoon prayers, and if she purifies herself before sunset, she prays the noon and afternoon prayers. Before dawn, the Maghrib and Isha prayers."
7284,"(7284) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, the same."
7285,"(7285) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Ata’, Peacock, and Mujahid. They said: If it flies before When the sun sets, she performs the noon and afternoon prayers, and if she performs ablution before dawn, she performs the sunset and evening prayers."
7286,"(7286) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, and Tawoos, that they said: If the menstruating woman purifies herself before sunset She bathed and prayed the noon and afternoon prayers, and if she purified herself before dawn, she bathed and prayed the sunset and evening prayers."
7287,"(7287) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a menstruating woman purifies herself from the end During the day, she prays the noon and afternoon prayers, and when she purifies herself at the end of the night, she prays the sunset and evening prayers."
7288,"(7288) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If she purifies herself at the end of the night, let her pray the prayer. her night, and when she is purified at the end of the day, she should pray the prayer of her day."
7289,"(7289) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: If she sees the birds before sunset, she prays the noon prayer. And the afternoon prayer, and if she sees it before dawn, she prays the sunset and evening prayers."
7290,"(7290) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: You should pray the prayer that was purified at its appointed time."
7291,"(7291) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ar-Rabi’, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If she saw the bird at the time of noon, she did not She takes a bath until the time for the afternoon and afternoon prayers begins."
7292,"(7292) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: Muhammad did not see any harm in a man leading the people in prayer, reciting from the Qur’an."
7293,"(7293) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: I heard Al-Qasim saying: A slave used to lead Aisha in reciting the Qur’an. The Qur’an"
7294,"(7294) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Urwa narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Malika, that Aisha She freed a slave of hers, and he used to lead her in prayer during Ramadan, reciting the Qur’an."
7295,"(7295) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Aisha ibn Talha, that she used to command A boy or a person who recites the Qur’an and leads it in prayer during Ramadan."
7296,"(7296) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hikam; Concerning a man who leads in prayer during Ramadan and recites from the Qur’an, it is permitted."
7297,"(7297) Abu Dawud al-Talisi told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of al-Hasan and Muhammad, who said: There is no harm in him."
7298,"(7298) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Rabah bin Abi Marouf, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in him."
7299,"(7299) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Rabi’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, saying: There is no harm in him leading in prayer with the Qur’an if he does not find one. It means one who recites outwardly."
7300,"(7300) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Issa bin Taman told us, he said: Thabit Al-Bunani told me, he said: It was Anas is praying and his servant is holding the Qur’an behind him, and when they discuss a verse, it is opened to him."
7301,"(7301) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyash al-Amiri, on the authority of Sulayman bin Hanzali al-Bakri, He passed by a man who was leading a group of people in the Qur’an, and he struck him with his foot."
7302,"(7302) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman, that he hated to be led in prayer. The Qur’an"
7303,"(7303) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he disliked for a man to lead in prayer reciting the Qur’an. To imitate the People of the Book."
7304,"(7304) Muhammad ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They hated that a man who was He reads from the Qur’an."
7305,"(7305) Al-Muharbibi told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, that he hated for a man to lead in prayer reciting the Qur’an."
7306,"(7306) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham al-Dastawai told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab, he said: If it was With him is someone who recites, they repeated it, but he did not recite the Qur’an."
7307,"(7307) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hisham al-Dastawai narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of al-Hasan, that he hated it, and he said: This is what Christians do."
7308,"(7308) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Hammad and his followers, about a man who led the people in Ramadan, in the Qur’an. His thoughts"
7309,"(7309) Israel told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: He does not recite the Qur’an in prayer."
7310,"(7310) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi? She prays until she has menstruated, and at the time of prayer she makes up for it if she becomes pure."
7311,"(7311) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Shubramah, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: If the time for prayer begins, the woman has her menstrual period. Before you pray, you should pray it when you purify yourself."
7312,"(7312) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Iyas, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I asked him, about A woman entered the time for prayer and delayed it until she had her period. He said: It begins with her when she becomes pure."
7313,"(7313) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad, who said: If she menstruates at the time of prayer, then it is not She must make up that prayer, unless the time has passed."
7314,"(7314) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, who said: She is not required to make up for it because she is in debt. time"
7315,"(7315) Ali bin Musahir narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Mu’adh al-Adawiyah, on the authority of Aisha, that The woman asked her if a menstruating woman could perform the prayer, and Aisha said to her: You are a free woman. We used to menstruate in the covenant of the Prophet. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, then we purify ourselves, but he does not order us to make up the prayers. (Bukhari 321, Abu Dawud 266)"
7316,"(7316) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Yazid al-Rashk, on the authority of Muadh al-Adawiya, she said: Aisha was asked, “Will you be rewarded?” The menstruating woman prayed, she said: The wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to menstruate, so should they be sufficient, meaning they should not make up for the period? (Muslim 2651, Ahmad 6/185)"
7317,"(7317) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: We were the daughters of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him and his wives embrace, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered them to make up for the fast, and not He ordered them to perform the prayers. (Abdul Razzaq 1279)"
7318,"(7318) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim and Al-Shu’abi, they said: No. A menstruating woman performs the prayer."
7319,"(7319) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: A menstruating woman does not make up for the prayer."
7320,"(7320) Waki` narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Kathir al-Nawa'i, who said: I asked Fatima bint Ali whether they fulfill the prayer. During your menstrual days, she said no."
7321,"(7321) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, in a menstruating woman she hears the prostration. He said: Do not make up for it. Because it does not fulfill the prayer."
7322,"(7322) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Whenever Ibn al-Zubayr stood for prayer As if it were a stick of humility. Mujahid said: And it was narrated that Abu Bakr was like that."
7323,"(7323) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Abdullah said: Perform the prayer, meaning Dwell in it."
7324,"(7324) Waki’ told us, on the authority of a man whom he named Hasan, or Sufyan, on the authority of Zubaid, who said: I saw Zazan praying. As if it were wood."
7325,"(7325) Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I saw Muslim bin Yassar praying as if he was a wad."
7326,"(7326) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, he said: When Abdullah stood up to pray, it was as if a garment had been thrown away."
7327,"(7327) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Abdullah said: Perform the prayer."
7328,"(7328) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Abdullah said: They recited the prayer. Zaidah said: So I said to Mansour: What does he mean by that? He said: He said: Mastery of it."
7329,"(7329) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he hated for a man to say: I pray and he says we pray."
7330,"(7330) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Tasbih is for men and applause is for women. (Bukhari 1203 and Abu Dawud 936)"
7331,"(7331) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nazra, on the authority of Abu Harairah, he said: The Prophet prayed, prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace. One day, when he stood up to say “Allahu Akbar,” he said: “The devil has made me forget any of my prayers, so glorify God.” For men and applause for women. (Tirmidhi 2787, Nasa’i 9409)"
7332,"(7332) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid al-Madani, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Tasbih is for men and applause is for women."
7333,"(7333) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Glorification in prayer For men and applause for women."
7334,"(7334) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid, who said: I asked permission to enter Ibn Abi Layla while he was praying, and he said the Sublime Subhanahu. With the boy, so he opened for me."
7335,"(7335) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A man asked for permission from Jabir bin Abdullah, so he said the tasbih, then he entered and sat down. Until he left."
7336,"(7336) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’ ibn Umar, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, who said: I saw Umar ibn Abdul Aziz He was praying in the mosque, and a person passed by him and he swore in it."
7337,"(7337) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: So, when a man is praying in his house, he says tasbih. And the woman’s permission to clap."
7338,"(7338) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Perhaps a person would come to Muhammad while he was praying. So he sees his shadow, and Muhammad points with his hand, Glory be to God."
7339,"(7339) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ziyad, who said: I entered upon Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d and he was... He was praying, and he said: Glory be to God, and when he left, he said: Tasbih is for men and applause is for women."
7340,"(7340) Ubaidah bin Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Tasbih is for men and applause is for women."
7341,"(7341) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Harith Al-Ukli, on the authority of Abdullah bin Naji, on the authority of Ali He said: Whenever I entered upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was praying, I would bow to him. (Ibn Majah 3708 and Ahmad 1/85)"
7342,"(7342) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, who said: I passed by Ibn Omar while he was praying. Then he rebuked me by praising Him."
7343,"(7343) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, that he used to say: In a menstruating woman, she cleans herself and takes A place during the times of prayer where you remember God."
7344,"(7344) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: It was said to Abu Qalab: The menstruating woman hears the call to prayer, so she performs ablution, says “Allahu Akbar” and says “Tasbih.” He said: We asked about that, but we found no basis for it."
7345,"(7345) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Suleiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, who said: We did not find any basis for it."
7346,"(7346) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said:"
7347,"(7347) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about it, what did they think about it?"
7348,"(7348) Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Ayyub, who said: Khalid bin Yazeed al-Sadfi narrated to me. On the authority of his father, on the authority of Uqba bin Aamir, that he used to order the menstruating woman at the time of prayer to perform ablution and sit. In the courtyard of the mosque, and remember God, and praise and glorify Him."
7349,"(7349) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: We command our women during menstruation to They perform ablution at the time of each prayer, then they sit and say “Tasbeeh” and remember Allah."
7350,"(7350) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: I heard him say about a menstruating woman Perform ablution at every prayer and remember God."
7351,"(7351) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: Whoever prays four after Isha' will be like our portion of Laylat Al-Qadr."
7352,"(7352) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Four nights after Isha are equivalent to the like of Laylat al-Qadr."
7353,"(7353) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abdul-Jabbar bin Abbas, on the authority of Qays bin Wahhab, on the authority of Murra, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Whoever prays four prayers after the evening prayer without separating between them with a salutation, they will be equal to the equivalent of the night of Laylat al-Qadr."
7354,"(7354) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid ibn Ayman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Tabi’, on the authority of Ka’b ibn Maati’, who said: Whoever prays four prayers after the evening prayer, it is good to bow and prostrate in them, they will be equal to the likes of Laylat al-Qadr."
7355,"(7355) Abdā narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ayman, on the authority of Tabi‘a, on the authority of Ka’b and the like."
7356,"(7356) Ali narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Four rak’ahs after the last night of Isha’, in the same position as they were. From the Night of Power."
7357,"(7357) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Bukair bin Amir, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Aswad, who said: Whoever prays four The last rak'ahs after Isha' are equivalent to those of Laylat al-Qadr."
7358,"(7358) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Shu’bi, the client of Ibn Abbas, who said: I prayed next to Ibn Abbas, so I cracked my fingers, and when I finished the prayer, he said: You have no right to crack your fingers while you are in the prayer."
7359,"(7359) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He hated for a man to snap his fingers. That is, while he was praying."
7360,"(7360) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, that he hated to snap his fingers, and he In prayer"
7361,"(7361) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: There are five things that shorten the prayer: stretching out, turning around, and turning over. Grits, obsessive thoughts, and cracking fingers."
7362,"(7362) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid that they He hates that a man cracks his fingers while he is praying."
7363,"(7363) Hushaym told us, he said: Husayn told us, he said: I asked Abraham about a man who saw blood on his garment, and he In the prayer, he said: If it is a lot, then let him drop the garment, and if it is a little, then let him continue with his prayer."
7364,"(7364) Hatim bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that when he was praying, he saw His garment was covered with blood, so he was able to put it on, but if he was not able to put it on, he went out and washed it, then came back and built on what he had done. He was praying."
7365,"(7365) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to shed a small amount of blood. And many of them."
7366,"(7366) Hatim bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If you see him and you have prayed some of your prayers, put on the garment. And continue in your prayers."
7367,"(7367) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I asked Hammad about a man who was praying and saw blood on his garment. He said: The garment on his behalf, I said: If there are only two garments, he said: He throws on one of them and wraps himself around the other. I asked the arbitrator, and he said something like that."
7368,"(7368) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, that he was praying and saw blood on his garment. So he placed it."
7369,"(7369) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Abu Majlaz, blood that appears on the garment. He said: If you say takbeer You entered the prayer, but you did not see anything, then I saw him after, so he completed the prayer."
7370,"(7370) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: If you see blood on your clothing, go and Your prayers"
7371,"(7371) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Abu al-Bakhtari, on the authority of the attack, he said: I said: By Abdullah bin Rabah: I see blood on my dress while I am praying. He said: Continue your prayer, and when you leave, wash it."
7372,"(7372) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Khasif Al-Jazari, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The sheikh was granted permission if He wanted to stand up for prayer and put his foot forward."
7373,"(7373) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali Al-Salami, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Ma’abad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Concerning a man who gets up to pray and advances one of his legs, thinks about it, and says: This is a cursed step. (Abu Dawud 643. Ibn Khuzaymah 772)"
7374,"(7374) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, he said: Abu Bakr told me about someone who told him that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade covering the mouth during prayer."
7375,"(7375) Al-Thaqafi narrated to me, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, that he hated for a man to cover his mouth while he was in it. Prayer"
7376,"(7376) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he hated to cover his mouth, and he In prayer"
7377,"(7377) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, on the authority of Ja’dah bin Hubaira, that he saw A man was praying, wearing a cloak and a turban, with which he covered his face, so he took his cloak and a turban and threw them from the behind him"
7378,"(7378) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I asked him about covering the mouth during prayer. And tawaaf is considered part of prayer and permitted as part of tawaaf."
7379,"(7379) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Mujbir, that Salem bin Abdullah was If a man sees his mouth covered while praying, he pulls the garment tightly until he removes it from his mouth."
7380,"(7380) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, that he disliked a man covering his mouth during prayer."
7381,"(7381) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of someone who heard Ibn Abi Layla say something similar."
7382,"(7382) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muslim bin Budil, that he hated to pray like this. And he placed the flowers of his garment on her lip."
7383,"(7383) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Bukair bin Amir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim and Al-Shu’bi that they hated to cover him. The man said it in prayer."
7384,"(7384) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Umari narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he disliked for a man to stammer in speech. Prayer"
7385,"(7385) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hisham al-Dastawai narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, and Ikrimah They disliked the man stammering during prayer."
7386,"(7386) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, that he disliked a man praying masked."
7387,"(7387) Waki’ told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham, that he disliked a man stammering during prayer."
7388,"(7388) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that it is disliked for a man to pray masked."
7389,"(7389) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, who said: It was disliked to fumble on three occasions in combat. And in funerals, and in prayer."
7390,"(7390) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ali, that he disliked wearing one’s nose while praying. And the mouth"
7391,"(7391) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his leaders; Concerning a man covering his nose during prayer, he said: Ikrimah told me that Ibn Abbas disliked the nose.
 His qatada said: Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, Al-Nakha’i, and Ata’ hated him, and Al-Hasan saw no harm in him.
 His leaders said: As for the mouth, I do not see anything wrong with it."
7392,"(7392) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Khalda, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, that he hated to cover his nose in water. Prayer"
7393,"(7393) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Hammad about his thoughts."
7394,"(7394) Hafs told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He hated to cover his nose and mouth. All of them, and he does not see any harm in covering his mouth but not his nose."
7395,"(7395) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Hamid bin Abi Rafi’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Ka’b, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid said that he disliked a woman praying while wearing a veil, or circumambulating while wearing a veil."
7396,"(7396) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, that he disliked a woman praying wearing a niqab."
7397,"(7397) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It was disliked for a woman to pray wearing a niqab."
7398,"(7398) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Damra bin Sa’id, he heard Abu Sa’id say: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace, regarding prayer after the afternoon prayer until sunset and after dawn prayer until sunrise. (Bukhari 1197, Muslim 567)"
7399,"(7399) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Nasr bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his grandfather Muadh Al-Qurashi said that he circumambulated the Kaaba with Muadh bin Afra after the afternoon prayer and after the dawn prayer, but he did not pray, so I asked him, and he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: There is no prayer after two prayers after lunch until the sun rises, and after the afternoon prayer until it sets. The sun (Tabarani 378, Ahmad 4/219)"
7400,"(7400) Abu Asama and Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Khubayb ibn Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Hafs ibn Asim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade two prayers, about praying after sunrise. Fajr until the sun rises and after the afternoon until the sun sets. (Bukhari 584, Ahmad 2/496)"
7401,"(7401) Abu Asama and Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Saad bin Sa’id, he said: Amr told me, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade two prayers, one prayer after the break of dawn until the sun rises and rises. For it rises between the horns of Satan and sets between the horns of Satan, and for prayer after the afternoon prayer until the sun sets. (Tahawi 303)"
7402,"(7402) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, on the authority of Wahb bin Al-Ajda’, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: There is no prayer after the afternoon prayer unless the sun is pure white. (Abu Dawud 1268. Ahmad 1/81)"
7403,"(7403) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Simmak, he said: I heard Al-Muhallab bin Abi Safari narrating, on the authority of Samarra. Ibn Jundub, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not pray, or he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade it. To pray after the Fajr prayer until the sun rises, for it rises on a horn, or between the horns of a devil. (Tahawi 152. Ahmad 5/15)"
7404,"(7404) Shababah told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu al-Tayyah, who said: I heard Hamran bin Aban speaking, on the authority of Mu’awiyah, He looked at people praying after the afternoon prayer, and said: You are praying a prayer that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, accompanied us, but what We saw him praying and he forbade it. (Ahmad 4/99)"
7405,"(7405) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hussein Al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade prayer after the afternoon prayer until the sun sets, and prayer after the dawn prayer until it rises. The sun"
7406,"(7406) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Musa ibn Ubaidah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade two prayers: a prayer after the morning prayer until the sun rises, and a prayer after the afternoon prayer until it sets. The sun (Bukhari 5850, Muslim 289)"
7407,"(7407) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He narrated to me. Men who were pleasing to Omar and who pleased them, with Omar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no prayer after Fajr prayer until the sun rises, and no prayer after the afternoon prayer until the sun sets. (Bukhari 581, Abu Dawud 1270)"
7408,"(7408) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Majir, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, who said: It is not valid to pray after the afternoon prayer until the sun sets. And after the morning until the sun rises, he said, and Omar used to beat about that."
7409,"(7409) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Shaddad, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazeed, On the authority of Al-Ashtar, he said: Khaled bin Al-Walid used to force people to pray after the afternoon prayer."
7410,"(7410) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah, that Umar disliked praying after the afternoon prayer. And I hate what Omar hated."
7411,"(7411) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, who said: I saw Omar seeing a man praying after The afternoon and hit him until his cloak fell off."
7412,"(7412) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Sara, who said: I asked Salim about praying after the afternoon prayer. He said: I do not like to begin a prayer until the sun sets."
7413,"(7413) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: It was disliked to pray after the afternoon prayer. Until the sun sets."
7414,"(7414) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu Jamra, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I saw Omar attacking Ali. The two rak'ahs after the afternoon prayer."
7415,"(7415) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, who said: I heard Ubayd Allah bin Rafi’ bin Khadij He narrates, on the authority of his father, who said: Omar bin Al-Khattab saw me one day while I was praying after the afternoon prayer, so he waited for me until I prayed, and he said: What is this prayer? I said: You preceded me in some of the prayers, and Omar said: If I had known that you would pray after the afternoon prayer, I would have done so and so I did."
7416,"(7416) Waki’ told us, he said: Thabit bin Amara told us, on the authority of Abu Tamim al-Hajjimi, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: I prayed With the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and with Abu Bakr, Omar and Othman, so there is no prayer after lunch until the sun rises. (Abu Dawud 1410, Ahmad 2/106)"
7417,"(7417) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, he said: It was The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prays two rak’ahs after every prescribed prayer, except Fajr and Asr. (Abu Dawud 1269. Ahmad 1/124)"
7418,"(7418) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib, he said: I saw Omar bin Al-Khattab The muqadir performs the two prostrations after the afternoon prayer, meaning the two rak'ahs."
7419,"(7419) Husayn bin Ali narrated to us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Suwayd, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Qubaysah. Ibn Jabir, they said: Omar used to perform the two rak’ahs after the afternoon prayer."
7420,"(7420) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mukhtar, he said: I asked Anas bin Malik about prayer after the afternoon prayer, and he said: It was Umar. He beats the hands during the prayer after the afternoon prayer."
7421,"(7421) Waki’ told us, he said: Abu Hilal told us, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: Two dates with butter I like To the prayer after the afternoon prayer."
7422,"(7422) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, on the authority of Yazid bin Talq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Al-Bilamani, on the authority of Amr bin Absa, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, is there anyone who pursues you closer to God than someone who pursues you? So he said: Yes. In the middle of the night, pray as you see fit until you pray the Fajr prayer, then finish it until the sun rises and as long as it lasts: it is as if it is a hijf until spread out, then pray as long as you see fit until the pillar stands on its shadow, then continue until the sun has set, for Hell will be half covered. daylight, then pray as long as you see fit until you pray the afternoon prayer, then finish it until the sun sets, for it rises between my horns. Satan and sojourns between the horns of Satan. (Nasa’i 1560. Ahmad 4/113)"
7423,"(7423) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: What the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, left behind. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, performed two rak’ahs after the afternoon prayer in my house. (Bukhari 591. Muslim 299)"
7424,"(7424) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, he said: I entered with Ibn Abbas on Muawiyah. So Mu'awiyah made him sit on the bed, then he said to him: What are the two rak'ahs that people pray after the afternoon prayer? We have not seen the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, may God’s prayers and peace be upon them, but he did not command them to do so. He said: That is what Ibn al-Zubair gives fatwas to the people. So he sent to Ibn al-Zubair. So he asked him, and he said: Aisha told me that, so he sent for Aisha, and she said: Umm Salama told me that, so he sent To Umm Salama, so she went with the Messenger, and he asked Umm Salama, and she said, may God have mercy on her, she did not want this, for I told her that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade them both.
 While the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in my house, he performed ablution for the afternoon prayer, and he had sent a courier and many The immigrants were with him, and he was concerned about their affairs when he knocked on the door and went out to them and prayed the noon prayer, then he sat down and divided what he had brought. He remained like that until he prayed the afternoon prayer. When he finished, Bilal saw him, so he established the prayer and prayed the afternoon prayer, then he entered my house and prayed it. Two rak'ahs. When he finished, I said: I did not see you praying two rak'ahs after the afternoon prayer. I did not see you praying them. He said: I was occupied with the matter of the messenger. I did not pray after noon, so I prayed with them.
 Ibn al-Zubayr said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led them in prayer, so I will lead them in prayer. (Abu Dawud 2167, Ahmad 6/311)"
7425,"(7425) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I saw Abu Burda bin Abi Musa praying after the afternoon prayer. Two rak'ahs"
7426,"(7426) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Al-Sha’athi, who said: I went out with my father and Amr bin Maymun. Al-Aswad bin Yazid and Abu Wael used to pray two rak’ahs after the afternoon prayer."
7427,"(7427) Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awan narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Al-Muntashir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, He used to pray two rak'ahs after the afternoon prayer, and he was told, and he said: If only I had not prayed them, then I saw something stolen. He would have been trustworthy, but I asked Aisha, and she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not abandon Two rak'ahs before dawn and two rak'ahs after the afternoon prayer."
7428,"(7428) Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awan narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Al-Muntashir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Talha. A servant of Shurayh, who said: Shurayh used to pray two rak’ahs after the afternoon prayer, which he learned from Masruq."
7429,"(7429) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, that Al-Zubayr and Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr used to pray two rak'ahs after the afternoon prayer."
7430,"(7430) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, that he prayed With a carpet, in two rows, two rak'ahs after the afternoon prayer."
7431,"(7431) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Talha bin Yahya narrated to us, saying: I heard Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utba, on the authority of Umm Salamah said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was busy performing the two rak’ahs after noon, so he prayed them after the afternoon prayer. (Ahmad 6/306, Tabarani 583)"
7432,"(7432) Ja’far bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Al-Siddiqa, the daughter of Al-Siddiq, narrated to me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not enter upon her after the afternoon prayer except that he prayed Two rak'ahs"
7433,"(7433) Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I asked Abu Juhayfy about them, and he said: : If it does not benefit you, it will not harm you."
7434,"(7434) Abdullah bin Numayr and Abu Asama narrated to us, saying: Ubaid Allah bin Omar narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: Do not be too late to pray when the sun rises or when it sets, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade That (Nasa’i 1546)"
7435,"(7435) Waki’ told us, he said: Musa bin Ali told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, he said: I heard him say For three hours, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us to pray or to bury our dead in them. When the sun rises brightly until it rises, and when it begins to set until it sets, and when the dawn rises until lean (Tirmidhi 1030 and Abu Dawud 3185)"
7436,"(7436) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The sun rises when it rises between Satan horned me. He said: We were forbidden from praying at sunrise and at sunset. (Abu Ali 4977, Bazar 1823)"
7437,"(7437) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Qays ibn Muslim, on the authority of Tariq ibn Shihab, on the authority of Bilal, he said: No He forbids prayer except at sunset, because it sets in the horn of Satan."
7438,"(7438) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me that people circumambulated At home after dawn, then they sat at the dhikr until when the sun had risen they stood up and prayed. Aisha said: They sat. Even when it was the hour in which prayer was disliked, they stood up and prayed."
7439,"(7439) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Bustam bin Muslim, on the authority of Abu Raja’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: He should not pray when the sun rises. And not when it sets, for it rises and sets in the horns of Satan, but when it is straight and lofty."
7440,"(7440) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ubaid bin Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Maqil, who said: Abu Masoud saw a man He prays at sunrise, or at the hour in which prayer is disliked. So he commanded a man and he prohibited it."
7441,"(7441) Abd al-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, that Shurayh saw a man praying when the sun was yellowing, and he said: Forbid this to pray, for this is an hour in which prayer is not permissible."
7442,"(7442) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwah told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Do not focus your prayers on the rising of the sun or its setting, for it rises with the horn of Satan. (Bukhari 582. An-Nasa’i 1551)"
7443,"(7443) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwah told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: If the veil of the sun appears, delay the prayer until it appears, and if the veil of the sun sets, delay the prayer until Absence (Bukhari 3272)"
7444,"(7444) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Issa bin Hamid al-Rasibi narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Hasan saying: They used to hate it. Praying at sunrise until it rises, and at sunset until it sets."
7445,"(7445) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Ibn Masoud said: I do not like to have With a man’s prayer when the sun turns yellow, two halves."
7446,"(7446) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Ifriqi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zayd, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: There is no prayer after the break of dawn except two rak’ahs before the dawn prayer. (Daraqutni 2. Abd al-Razzaq 4757)"
7447,"(7447) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Muhammad Al-Yamami, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Omar, and Ibn Abbas, They said: There is no prayer after the break of dawn except the two rak’ahs of dawn."
7448,"(7448) Hushaym told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he said: There is no prayer after two rak’ahs. Fajr until you pray Fajr."
7449,"(7449) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, who said: Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab saw me while I was praying. Some of the night prayers that I missed after dawn came, so he said: Did you not know that prayer is disliked during this hour, except for two rak’ahs? Before Fajr prayer."
7450,"(7450) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to hate, when dawn came, to pray except Two rak'ahs"
7451,"(7451) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to dislike the prayer after two rak’ahs. dawn until they pray the prescribed prayer."
7452,"(7452) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: Whoever wishes to pray after When dawn comes, let him do it."
7453,"(7453) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: After the break of dawn, it is a good part, and it was It is recited after dawn with Al-Baqarah."
7454,"(7454) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Mansour bin Al-Ashl Al-Ghadani, who said: Abu Husayn asked Al-Shu’abi while I was listening. On the authority of a man who had some of his rosary remaining while he was praying and dawn had come, so he said: He should recite what was left of his rosary."
7455,"(7455) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I saw Abu Ishaq and Al-Hakam praying after dawn had broken."
7456,"(7456) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, who said: I saw Abd al-Rahman bin Awf and Ubayy bin Ka’b when the muezzin called the call to prayer. For the Maghrib prayer, they stood up and prayed two rak'ahs."
7457,"(7457) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, who said: He was asked about the two rak’ahs before sunset, and he said: I saw them when The muezzin called the call to prayer. They set out for the pillars and prayed."
7458,"(7458) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, on the authority of Abi, so he visited him, he said: I asked Anas, about The two rak'ahs before sunset, and he said: We used to perform them early at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Bukhari 625, Abu Dawud 1276)"
7459,"(7459) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: I saw Ibn Abi Layla praying two rak’ahs before Morocco"
7460,"(7460) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib Ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla. He said: I noticed the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying at every call to prayer."
7461,"(7461) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Khams, on the authority of Ibn Buraida, on the authority of Abdullah bin al-Mughaffal, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: There is a prayer between every two calls to prayer. Between every two calls to prayer there is a prayer between every two calls to prayer. A prayer for those who I wish (Bukhari 627. Muslim 304)"
7462,"(7462) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mughaffal, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. (Bukhari 624, Abu Dawud 1277)"
7463,"(7463) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ibrahim, who said: Tamim bin Salam, or Salam bin Tamim, said to Al-Hasan: What It says about the two rak'ahs before sunset, and he said: Two beautiful good deeds for those whom God wills for them."
7464,"(7464) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: I have never seen a jurist Anyone who prays before sunset except Saad bin Abi Waqqas."
7465,"(7465) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I heard a sheikh with Wasit saying: I heard Tawus saying: I asked Ibn Umar about The two rak'ahs before sunset, but he did not prohibit them."
7466,"(7466) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Kharijiyah ibn Mus`ab, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, on the authority of Ata` ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of God said: God: Images do not receive other images."
7467,"(7467) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Abraham was sitting with his back to the direction of Allah, and a man He was standing and praying for his future, so Abraham took his hand to protect himself from this side and from that side."
7468,"(7468) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hanzali al-Jumahi narrated to us, on the authority of Tawus, that a man vowed to prostrate on his forehead. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to him, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sat facing the direction of the people. Then the man stood behind him. And he said, “This is what he wore on his forehead,” so he prostrated on it."
7469,"(7469) Waki’ told us, he said: Abdullah bin Ma’dan Abu Ma’dan told us, he said: I heard a peacock narrating this hadith. He added more to it, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: You have fulfilled your vow. (Nasa’i 7630, Ahmad 214)"
7470,"(7470) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, that he used to run to prayer."
7471,"(7471) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I saw Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid hastened to the prayer."
7472,"(7472) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ibn Juraij narrated to us, on the authority of a man from the people of Medina, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he was He jogs to prayer."
7473,"(7473) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi`, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he heard the iqama in al-Baqi` and hurried. Walking"
7474,"(7474) Waki` narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, who said: I saw Sa`id bin Jubayr running to Prayer"
7475,"(7475) Ubaidah bin Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, who said: I saw Saeed bin Jubayr running to Prayer"
7476,"(7476) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Qays Al-Mala’i, on the authority of Salma bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Amara bin Umair said: Abdullah said: The most worthy of what we seek is prayer."
7477,"(7477) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Ubaidullah, he said: I saw Ibn Umar running to The mosque is in an eclipse, and with it are its sandals."
7478,"(7478) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah who narrated it, he said: When you have come to prayer, do not perform it while you are striving, but perform it while remaining still. So whatever you catch up with, then pray and whatever you have missed. So pay up. (Bukhari 636 and Abu Dawud 573)"
7479,"(7479) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Omar bin Abi Salama, on the authority of my father Hariri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When you perform the prayer, perform it with dignity and tranquility. Whatever you have reached, pray, and whatever you have missed, complete. (Bukhari 636. Tirmidhi 327)"
7480,"(7480) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Dharr, who said: If the prayer is established So walk towards it as you used to walk, and complete what you have reached and fulfill what came before you."
7481,"(7481) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: If it is fixed with prayer, then walk with it upon you. Tranquility and dignity, so pray what you have attained and fulfill what came before you. (Muslim 154)"
7482,"(7482) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Go to prayer, take close steps, and remember Allah."
7483,"(7483) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Mas’udi told us, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Aqmar, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, he said: Abdullah said: You have seen us, and we are approaching the steps to prayer."
7484,"(7484) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ja’far bin Hayyan Abu Al-Ashhab narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit Al-Bunani, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, He said: I went out with Zaid bin Thabit to the mosque, so I quickly walked and he locked me up."
7485,"(7485) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Dawud bin Faraij, he said: Mawla Sufyan bin Ziyad narrated to me, He was going to the mosque in a hurry. He said: Then Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam joined me and said: I mean... Your walk, for in prayer you will not take a step except that God will raise you in rank because of it, and remove from you a sin because of it."
7486,"(7486) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of the hostages of Banu Abdullah, she said: I heard the Iqama, so I hurried and passed by Ali bin Hussein while I was hastening. He pulled my garment and said: Go on your messengers."
7487,"(7487) Yahya bin Ali told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, who said: I and a companion of mine returned Mujahid, and I attended the prayer. He said: Go and pray, and walk at your own pace. Whatever you catch up with the imam, pray, and whatever you miss, complete."
7488,"(7488) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn Khalidah, who said: I was walking with Ibn Umar. To the prayer, and if an ants had walked with him, she would have seen that he would not precede her."
7489,"(7489) Yazeed bin Harun told us, he said: Humaid al-Tawil told us, on the authority of Thabit, he said: Anas took him by the hand and made He walked slowly to the prayer, then he turned to me and said: This is what Zayd bin Thabit used to do so that his mistakes would be many."
7490,"(7490) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Thabit ibn Ubaid, on the authority of Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: They brought me wine from the mosque, and I said: I am menstruating. He said, “Your menstruation is not In your hand (Muslim 244. Tirmidhi 134)"
7491,"(7491) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Ibn Umar was asked about a menstruating woman handling birds or something. From the mosque, and he said: Her menstruation is not within her control."
7492,"(7492) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in a menstruating woman putting something in the mosque and taking it. From it, and do not enter it."
7493,"(7493) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, that he did not think it was wrong for a menstruating woman to give birth in the mosque. Whatever she wants and she can take it from him."
7494,"(7494) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of his leaders, who said: A menstruating woman should be taken from the mosque, and not placed. Therein"
7495,"(7495) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Hakim, on the authority of Jeddah Al-Rabbab, that Uthman bin Hanif said: My maid, give me the wine. She said: I am not praying. He said: Your menstrual period is not in your hand."
7496,"(7496) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to say to his female servant: Give me the wine from the mosque. You say: I am menstruating. He says: You are not in control of your menstruation."
7497,"(7497) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A menstruating woman may take from The mosque and put in it."
7498,"(7498) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ataa: In a menstruating woman, she takes something from the mosque. He said: Yes. Except the Qur’an."
7499,"(7499) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he saw no harm in a menstruating woman taking anything. From the mosque and put it in it."
7500,"(7500) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, he said: Abu Wael used to send his menstruating servant to Abu Razin. Then you bring him the Qur’an from him, and he keeps his relationship with it."
7501,"(7501) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm for a man to take the Qur’an if it is in his bowl, or With his relationship"
7502,"(7502) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Abu Khaled al-Dalani, on the authority of al-Qasim, meaning the lame, who said: I saw Sa`id bin Jubayr read from the Qur’an, then handed it to a boy of his who was a Magian according to his relationship."
7503,"(7503) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ayman bin Nabul, who said: I heard Ata’ say: There is no harm in a menstruating woman having intercourse with her. The Qur’an"
7504,"(7504) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, that he did not see any harm in a man altering the Qur’an. And he is not pure."
7505,"(7505) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Salih, on the authority of Ghalib Abi al-Dhayl, who said: Abu Razin ordered me to open The Qur’an was not covered with ablution, so I asked Abraham what he thought about it."
7506,"(7506) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Ubaidullah bin Omar narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, that he did not touch the Qur’an. Except that He is pure."
7507,"(7507) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he saw no harm in it."
7508,"(7508) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I asked Amir about touching the Qur’an without ablution, and he said: No. It's okay
 Muhammad bin Ali, Abd al-Rahman bin al-Aswad, al-Qasim, Salem and Tawoos disliked it."
7509,"(7509) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ubaid Allah ibn Umar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Umar said: What is between The East and the West before you."
7510,"(7510) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: Omar said: What is between the East and the West before? You faced the Qiblah."
7511,"(7511) Waki’ told us, he said: Malik bin Mughul told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: What Between the East and the West before him."
7512,"(7512) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Mas’udi told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: When you make Maghrib To your right and the east to your left, and whatever is between them is for the people of the north."
7513,"(7513) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-A’la bin Amir al-Thaalabi, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Salami, On the authority of Ali, he said: What is between the East and the West is before me."
7514,"(7514) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: What is between the East and the West before?"
7515,"(7515) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Hakim bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibrahim. And Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, who said: What is between the East and the West is before me."
7516,"(7516) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha’, on the authority of a man who named him, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: What is between the East and the West before?"
7517,"(7517) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amri told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, on the authority of Omar, he said: Between the East And the Maghrib is before it."
7518,"(7518) Al-Mu’alla bin Mansour narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Ja’far narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman bin Muhammad Al-Akhnasi, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: What is between the East and the West is before me. (Hakim 205)"
7519,"(7519) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Abdul Rahman Al-Hashemi, who said: The first time mosques were created, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw dirt in the mosque and rubbed it off, then he ordered someone to clean it and smear its place. He said: So people created mosques. (Abu Dawud 482)"
7520,"(7520) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw before him The mosque was empty, so he got up to it and rubbed it with his hand, then called for a polite person, and said: Aamir is of the same age."
7521,"(7521) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, that when Ibn Zubayr built the Ka’bah, he covered its walls. With musk"
7522,"(7522) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwah told us, on the authority of his father, he said: The command of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace By building mosques in homes and ordering them to be cleansed and perfumed, meaning the tribes. (Abu Dawud 4561, Ibn Majah 759)"
7523,"(7523) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amri told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, that Omar ibn Al-Khattab used to stone the mosque. In every gathering."
7524,"(7524) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Suleiman, who said: I saw Abraham seeing the mosque being created and there was no defect in it. That"
7525,"(7525) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace A slug crawled in front of the mosque. (Bukhari 4071, Muslim 549)"
7526,"(7526) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ali bin al-Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: I was informed that Abu Al-Darda' saw a slug across the wall of the mosque and scratched it."
7527,"(7527) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Iyad bin Abdullah bin Saad bin Abi Sarh, on the authority of Abu Saeed said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the mosque with a limp in his hand, and he loved ascensers, and he saw He put his nose in the kiss and rubbed it, then he turned to the people and said: O people, when one of you stands and prays, God will meet him. And on his right is an angel. Would any of you like a man to meet him and spit in his face, but not one of you? towards the direction, nor from his right, and let him spit under his left foot, or from his left, if you hasten it, he hastened Let him say this, meaning about his garment. (Abu Dawud 481. Ahmad 3/24)"
7528,"(7528) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim ibn Mihran, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he saw Nakhama facing the mosque, so he turned to the people with his face, and said: What is the matter with any of you? He stands facing his Lord and slanders before Him. Would any of you like to face him and slander before Him? If one of you has his hair wet, let him wash his hair, on his left hand, or under his feet, but if that is not possible, let him say thus about his garment, then Ismail showed us that he spit on his garment, then rubbed it. (Muslim 389. An-Nasa’i 298)"
7529,"(7529) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a person sitting in the mosque. So he wiped it, then said: If one of you spits, he should not spit on his forehead, nor on his right, but rather he should spit on his His left hand, or under his feet, or to make, or to say thus, then he spit on the edge of his garment, then he returned it to him. (Bukhari 417, Darmi 1396)"
7530,"(7530) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hamid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He saw sputum in front of the mosque, so he rubbed it with his pebbles, and said: If any of you spits, let him not spit. between his hands, nor on his right, nor on his left. (Bukhari 414, Muslim 52)"
7531,"(7531) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ruba’i, on the authority of Tariq bin Abdullah Al-Muharbiy, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: When you pray, do not spit between your hands or on your right, but Spit, on your left, or under your foot. (Tirmidhi 571, Abu Dawud 479)"
7532,"(7532) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Hudhayfah, who said: If a Muslim slave performs ablution So he performed his ablution well, then he stood up and prayed, may God face him until he was the one who left, or If something bad happens, it does not spit between his hands, nor from his right hand, for from his right hand he writes down good deeds, but He spits, to his left, or behind his back."
7533,"(7533) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Hudhayfah, that he had narrated something similar to this. (Ibn Majah 1023)"
7534,"(7534) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Adiy bin Thabit, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Hudhayfy, he said: Whoever prays So he spit out facing the qiblah, and his spit will come in his face on the Day of Resurrection. (Bazzar 411)"
7535,"(7535) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Suqi, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: If he spits in the kissel, it comes I will be as hot as you will be on the Day of Resurrection until it falls between his eyes. (Tabarani 7960)"
7536,"(7536) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It was disliked for a man to spit between His hand during prayer, or on his right, and he said: spit, on your left, or under your feet."
7537,"(7537) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Muhammad hated for a man to jump towards the qiblah, and on the authority of His right hand"
7538,"(7538) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he hated to jump towards the qiblah. He said: He was Ibn Sirin hates both kisses."
7539,"(7539) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Ubaid Allah bin Omar narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, he saw his nose blowing in front of the mosque, so he went to it, then he said: When one of you stands during a prayer, he should not blow his nose on the face of the mosque. His face, for God is before the face of any of you when he is in prayer. (Bukhari 4061 Muslim 50)"
7540,"(7540) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. In a manner of speaking (Bukhari 1213. Muslim 388)"
7541,"(7541) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Spitting in the mosque is a sin and its expiation is to hide it. (Bukhari 1214, Muslim 55)"
7542,"(7542) Zaid bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Hussein bin Waqid, on the authority of Abu Ghalib, on the authority of Abu Imamah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: A slug in a mosque is a sin, but burying it well is a sin. (Ahmad 5/2601 Tabarani 8091)"
7543,"(7543) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, that Abu Ubaidah came to his residence and had He spit in the mosque and was about to bury her until he came to his house, so he mentioned and brought a lamp until he saw her."
7544,"(7544) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, on the authority of Makhoul, that Ibn Umar sneezed, or spit in water. The mosque and he forgot to hide her until he came to her house, so he remembered after she had left, so he returned with a lamp and sought her out in the mosque. Until he saw her, then he said: Whoever spits in the mosque is a sin and his repentance is that he hides her."
7545,"(7545) Muhammad bin Fudayl and Abdou told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Azhar, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Al-Bazzaq In the mosque is a sin and its expiation is to hide it."
7546,"(7546) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: A slug in the mosque is a sin. He said: So I mentioned that to Al-Nakha’i, and he said: It used to be said, his atonement is his burial."
7547,"(7547) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Awwam, on the authority of Ibn Abi Al-Dhudhail, who said: A slug in the mosque is a sin. And atonement for it, we buried it."
7548,"(7548) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Saif bin Sulaiman al-Makki narrated to us, saying: I heard Mujahid saying: Bazaq Abu Ubaidah Ibn al-Jarrah was in the mosque at night and did not know where it was, so he went out and brought the lamp and looked for it until he saw it."
7549,"(7549) Waki’ told us, he said: Mis’ar told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Mulqat, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The mosque To shed mucus or pituitary fluid, just as the skin sheds in fire."
7550,"(7550) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Wasmiy, on the authority of a man called Ziyad, a man from Banu Fazara. He heard Abu Hurairah say: The mosque is emptied of the pituitary substance, just as a piece of cloth or skin is emptied of Fire"
7551,"(7551) Waki’ told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Laith, he said: I have never seen a peacock spit in the mosque, nor did it touch it. Gravel, and do not recline on it."
7552,"(7552) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Al-Rukain, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Asmaa bin Al-Hakam, he said: I asked about everything, even breathing in the mosque, and it was said: Its expiation is burying it."
7553,"(7553) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad, on the authority of Amer bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of Abi Saad, who said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: If one of you sniffs his nose in the mosque Let him hide it, and do not strike the skin or clothing of a believer and thus harm him. (Ahmad 1/1791, Ibn Khuzaymah 1311)"
7554,"(7554) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Abu Mawdud narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Hadrad al-Aslami, on the authority of Abu Hariri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If one of you spits in my mosque, or says in the mosque Let him dig, let him shine, or let him spit on a garment until he brings it out. (Abu Dawud 478. Ahmad 2/324)"
7555,"(7555) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Hassan bin Atiyya, who said: Muadh bin Jabal used to take A flea during prayer, and he rubs it with his hand until it kills it, then spits on it."
7556,"(7556) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Aswad, he said: It was Omar bin Al-Khattab killed lice while praying until their blood appeared on his hand."
7557,"(7557) Abdi told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ziyad bin Anam, on the authority of Muslim bin Yasar, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab; Concerning a man who picks up a lice while he is praying, he said: He takes it away and throws it away."
7558,"(7558) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who finds lice while praying, he said: Bury them."
7559,"(7559) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If he kills her during prayer, then there is nothing wrong."
7560,"(7560) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Thawr al-Shami narrated to us, on the authority of Rashid bin Saad, on the authority of Malik bin Yakhamir, who said: Thawr passed away Rashid bin Saad, or someone else, said: I saw Muadh bin Jabal killing lice and fleas during prayer."
7561,"(7561) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, who said: I said to Abraham: Do I remove lice while I am praying? He said: Bury it in the gravel. Indeed, the earth has been made as a burial ground for the living and the dead."
7562,"(7562) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak; Concerning a man who kills lice while praying, he said: There is no harm in it."
7563,"(7563) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Thawair, on the authority of Mujahid; Concerning a man who finds lice while praying, he said: There is no harm in him turning them around."
7564,"(7564) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir; Concerning a man who finds lice while praying, he said: He leaves it."
7565,"(7565) Hammad bin Khalid narrated to us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Sadiqa Abu Touba, on the authority of Anas, that it was Lice is killed during prayer."
7566,"(7566) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ali bin Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Al-Hadrami bin Later, on the authority of a man from the Ansar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If one of you finds lice in the mosque Let him wrap her in his garment until he brings her out. (Ahmad 410, Bayhaqi 294)"
7567,"(7567) Jarir told us, on the authority of Qaboos, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Concerning a man who finds lice while he is in the mosque. He said: He buries them in the gravel. He said: And I saw Abu Dhabyan do that. That"
7568,"(7568) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Muslim Al-Mala’i, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Khathim, that Abdullah was buried He prayed in the mosque, then recited: {Have We not made the earth a level surface}."
7569,"(7569) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, on the authority of a man, who said: I saw a father in front of him. He will spit in the mosque and bury you there."
7570,"(7570) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Aban bin Abdullah Al-Bajli narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Muslim Al-Tha’labi, who said: I saw the father of an imam spitting in his mosque, and he He buries lice in the gravel."
7571,"(7571) Waki’ told us, he said: Abu Khalda told us, he said: I saw Abu Al-Aaliya burying the lice in the mosque and reciting : {Have We not made the earth a level surface?}"
7572,"(7572) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Abi Arouba told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, he said, “Bury her in The mosque may bury something worse, including: pituitary gland."
7573,"(7573) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ali, he said: I saw Ibn Maqil wandering around in The mosque. My grandmother was the mother of a son of Al-Hasan bin Ali, and he used to isolate himself from her."
7574,"(7574) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muslim, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, he said: I took from Ibn Omar brought a beast while he was praying in the mosque, so I threw it in the direction of the mosque, but that did not bother him."
7575,"(7575) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If you catch lice while you are in the mosque So bury her in gravel."
7576,"(7576) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Yusuf ibn Mahak, who said: I saw Ibn Umayr take some of Ibn"
7577,"(7577) Qattan bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ghalib, who said: I saw the father of his imam taking the lice and throwing it in it. The mosque, so I said: O Abu Imamah, do you take the lice and throw them in the mosque? He said: {Have We not made the earth as a surface of living beings? And dead}"
7578,"(7578) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Hani bin Urwah al-Muradi, on the authority of Abd Al-Hamid bin Mahmoud said: We prayed behind one of the princes, but the people forced us until we prayed between the two pillars. When we prayed, Anas bin Malik said: We used to fear this during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Abu Dawud 673. Ahmad 3/131)"
7579,"(7579) Hushaym told us, he said: Khaled told us about the one who told him, on the authority of Anas, he said he forbade us to pray between the two pillars."
7580,"(7580) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Maadi Karb, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: No. Arrange among the camps, and do not follow a people who dispute and confuse you. (Abdul Razzaq 2487. Tabarani 9295)"
7581,"(7581) Fudayl bin Iyad narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn bin Hilal, on the authority of Hudhayfah, that he disliked praying between people. The masters"
7582,"(7582) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayoub Abi Al-Ala, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Qur’a, on the authority of his father, he said: He saw me. Omar, I was praying between two pillars, so he took my back and brought me closer to a curtain, and said: Pray towards it."
7583,"(7583) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he disliked praying between the lords, and he said: Complete."
7584,"(7584) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hasan bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Do not pray between The masters"
7585,"(7585) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he saw no harm in lining up between the pillars."
7586,"(7586) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: I do not know of any problem with praying between the pillars."
7587,"(7587) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Waqa’i, he said: Saeed bin Jubayr used to lead us between two posts."
7588,"(7588) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, who said: I saw Ibrahim al-Taymi leading the prayer. His people are between two cylinders."
7589,"(7589) Waki’ told us, Musa bin Nafi’ told us, he said: I saw Saeed bin Jubair leading us between the two pillars."
7590,"(7590) Waki’ narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Bishr ibn Tu’ma al-Thawri, who said: I saw al-Rabi’ ibn Khathim praying in His illness is between two pillars and depends on one of them."
7591,"(7591) Waki’ narrated to us, Sufyan and Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdul-Ala, he said: Suwayd bin He neglected to lead us between two pillars."
7592,"(7592) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: Yahya bin Wattab used to lead us between two pillars."
7593,"(7593) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Rabi’ah ibn Uthman al-Taymi, who said: Idris al-Sana’ani narrated to us, on the authority of a man, who is called Hamdan was the letter of the people of Yemen to Omar. He said: Omar said: Those who pray are more deserving of the pillars than those who speak to them."
7594,"(7594) Hushaym bin Bashir narrated to us, saying: Husayn informed us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Talha bin Rukkani al-Muttalibi, on the authority of Jubair bin Mutim said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: One prayer in this mosque of yours is better than a thousand prayers. Everything else except the Sacred Mosque. (Taalisi 950, Ahmad 4/80)"
7595,"(7595) Abu Asama told us, he said: Abdullah bin Omar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace be upon him: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in any other place except the Sacred Mosque. (Muslim 1013. Ahmad 6/53)"
7596,"(7596) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, that he heard Abu Salamah narrate to Al-Aghar, that he heard Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: One prayer in this mosque of yours is better than a thousand Prayer in other mosques except the Kaaba. (Bukhari 1190, Tirmidhi 325)"
7597,"(7597) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, Musa ibn Ubaidah informed us, on the authority of Dawud ibn Mudarrak, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: One prayer in my mosque is better than a thousand prayers in other mosques. Except the Sacred Mosque. (Bazzar 1193)"
7598,"(7598) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid bin Sakhr, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: Whoever comes to this mosque of mine has not come to it except for what is good, that it may be taught to him, or Whoever learns it, then he is in the position of a Mujahid in the path of God, and whoever comes to him for other than that, then he is in the position of a man. To the enjoyment of others. (Ahmad 2/418 and Ibn Hibban 87)"
7599,"(7599) Shababah bin Suwar narrated to us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Ma’abad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Maimunah, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Prayer in it, meaning a mosque. Medina is better than a thousand prayers in any other place except the mosque of Mecca. (Muslim 510)"
7600,"(7600) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Saad, on the authority of Sulayman bin Uthman, who heard Ibn al-Zubayr saying: I heard Umar say One prayer in this mosque is better than a hundred prayers elsewhere."
7601,"(7601) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Anis bin Abi Yahya, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, He said: You saw a man from Banu Khudri and a man from Banu Amr bin Awf in the mosque that was founded on piety. Al-Khudri said: It is the mosque of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Al-Awfi said: It is the mosque of Qubay, so they came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, and he said: This is this, meaning his mosque, and in that there is much good. (Tirmidhi 323. Ahmad 3/23)"
7602,"(7602) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Sa`id al-Khudri, on the authority of his father, He said: The mosque that was founded on piety is the mosque of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
7603,"(7603) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Uthman, who said: Imran bin Abi Anas told me, on the authority of Saul bin Sa’d, he said: Two men disagreed about the mosque that was founded on piety, and one of them said: It is the Mosque of Medina, and the other said: It is the Mosque of Medina. Quba’, so he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: This is your mosque. (Ahmad 5/331, Ibn Hibban 1605)"
7604,"(7604) Waki’ narrated to us, Rabi’i bin Uthman narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The mosque that It was founded on piety and is the Mosque of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
7605,"(7605) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad, on the authority of Kharijiyah bin Zayd, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace And he said: The mosque that was founded on piety from the first day is the mosque of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Tabarani 4854)"
7606,"(7606) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: The Great Mosque of Medina."
7607,"(7607) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid bin Sakhr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: I entered upon The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I asked him about the mosque that was founded on piety. He took a handful of pebbles, then struck With this land, he said: This is it, meaning the Mosque of Medina. (Muslim 1015. Ahmad 3/24)"
7608,"(7608) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ibn Harmala, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, who said: It is the mosque of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted you."
7609,"(7609) Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amir, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Anas, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, on the authority of Abi bin Kaab, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: The mosque that was founded on piety is my mosque. (Ahmad 5/1168 Hakim 334)"
7610,"(7610) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar, he said: Abu Al-Abarad, the client of Banu Khatmah, narrated to us that He heard Usayd bin Dhahir Al-Ansari, who was one of the companions of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, speaking on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: A prayer in the Quba Mosque is like Umar. (Bukhari 1641, Ibn Majah 1411)"
7611,"(7611) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, he said: Yusuf bin Taman informed me, on the authority of my father. Umamah bin Sahl, on the authority of Abi Sahl bin Hanif, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever performs ablution does well. He performed his ablution, then he came to the Quba Mosque and prayed four rak’ahs there. That was the justice of his life. (Bukhari 3389. Ahmad 3/487)"
7612,"(7612) Abu Asama told us, Ubad Allah ibn Umar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, he came to the Quba Mosque, walking and riding. (Bukhari 1194 and Abu Dawud 2033)"
7613,"(7613) Abu Khaled Sulayman bin Hayyan told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Salit bin Saad, he said: I heard Ibn Umar He says whoever goes out wanting a qaba and does not want anything else, so praying in it was like an Umrah."
7614,"(7614) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hashim bin Hashim, on the authority of Aisha bint Saad, she said: I heard my father saying, “Let me pray.” I love the Quba Mosque more than praying in Bayt al-Maqdis."
7615,"(7615) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Salih Al-Hanafi, on the authority of his brother Taliq Ibn Qays, he said: Abu Dharr said: Because praying on red sand is more beloved to me than praying in Bayt al-Maqdis."
7616,"(7616) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Hudhayfah, who said: If I walked until there was no There is only a farsakh between me and the Holy House, or two farsakhs. I have not come to it, or I have not liked to have come to it."
7617,"(7617) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Miqdam, on the authority of Hibba, who said: A man came to Ali and said: I am I bought a camel and got ready and wanted the Holy House, so he said: Sell your camel and pray in this mosque, meaning a mosque. Kufa, there is no mosque more beloved to me than the Sacred Mosque and the Mosque of Medina, and it has subtracted from its foundations five hundred cubits. It means the Kufa Mosque."
7618,"(7618) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: Ka'b met me at the Holy House and said: Where are you from? So I said: From the Kufa Mosque, and he said: Because I came from where I came is more beloved to me than giving a thousand dinars in charity, putting each A dinar from it was in the hand of a poor person, then he swore that the middle of the earth was like the bottom of a basin."
7619,"(7619) Yahya bin Ya’li told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Qaz’a, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Travels should only be made to three mosques: the Grand Mosque, the Medina Mosque, and the Bayt al-Maqdis Mosque. (Bukhari 1197, Muslim 416)"
7620,"(7620) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Do not embark on journeys except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, this mosque of mine, and Al-Aqsa Mosque. (Bukhari 1189. Ahmad 2/234)"
7621,"(7621) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Talq, on the authority of Qaz’a, who said: I asked Ibn Umar who came to the Mount, and he said: Leave the Mount and do not He came and said: Do not embark on a journey except to three mosques."
7622,"(7622) Yahya bin Al-Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Dhayl, who said: Journeys are only undertaken to the ancient House."
7623,"(7623) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: No saddlebags should be set out except for three people. Mosques"
7624,"(7624) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, Ja’far bin Ibrahim from the descendants of Dhul-Janahayn narrated to us, he said: Ali bin Omar narrated to me, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hussein, that he saw a man coming to a place that was at the grave of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace be upon him, entered it and made supplication. So he called him and said: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith that I heard from my father, on the authority of my grandfather, on the authority of the Messenger of God? God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not take my grave as a place of rest, nor take your homes as graves, and pray for me, for your prayer is And your greeting will reach me wherever you are. (Bukhari 1868 Abu Ali 6728)"
7625,"(7625) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of Hasan ibn Hasan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Do not take my grave as a place of rest, nor take your homes as graves, but pray for me wherever you are, for your prayers are You inform me. (Abdul Razzaq 6726)"
7626,"(7626) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Oh God, do not make my grave an idol to be prayed to. God’s wrath is intense against a people who have taken the graves of their prophets as places of worship. (Imam Malik 85)"
7627,"(7627) Muadh bin Muadh told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: It has reached Omar bin Al-Khattab that people are coming The tree under which he was sold, he said, so he ordered it to be cut down."
7628,"(7628) Zakaria bin Adiy told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Amr, on the authority of Zayd bin Abi Anisa, on the authority of Amr bin Murah On the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith Al-Najrani, he said: Jundub narrated to me, saying: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, before He dies with five and says: Indeed, those before you used to lie in the graves of their prophets and righteous people. Places of worship: Do not take graves as places of worship. Indeed, I forbid you from that. (Muslim 23. Tabarani 1686)"
7629,"(7629) Hashim bin Al-Qasim narrated to us, Shaiban narrated to us, on the authority of Hilal bin Abi Hamid Al-Ansari, on the authority of Urwah bin Al-Zubair, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said during his illness from which he did not get up: May God curse him. The Jews and Christians used the graves of their prophets as mosques.
 Had it not been for that, his grave would have been exposed, but he feared that it would be used as a mosque. (Bukhari 1390, Muslim 19)"
7630,"(7630) Wakī’ narrated to us, Hisham bin Urwah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that they discussed with the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him during his illness, and Umm Salamah, or the mother of her beloved, mentioned a church she had seen in the land of Abyssinia. There are pictures in it, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: These are the people who, when a righteous man was among them and he died, built upon Ali. He made his grave a mosque and depicted it. Those are the worst of creation. (Bukhari 434, Muslim 16)"
7631,"(7631) Wakī’ narrated to us, Shu’bā’ narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Jahadī al-Awdi, who said: I heard Abu Salih after he grew up. He narrates, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed women who visit graves and those who go to mosques over them. And the lamps. (Tirmidhi 320, Abu Dawud 3228)"
7632,"(7632) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Ma’roor bin Suwayd, who said: We went out with Omar during his Hajj, and he performed Hajj, so he recited. Us at dawn: (Have you not seen how your Lord dealt with the companions of the elephant), and (to the thousands of Quraysh) When he completed his Hajj and returned with the people They started, so he said: What is this? They said: A mosque in which the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed. Then he said: This is how the People of the Book perished. They took traces of Their Prophets are a trade: whoever of you has offered the opportunity to pray, let him pray, and whoever of you has not offered the opportunity to pray, let him pray. He prays"
7633,"(7633) Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: They hated to change the traces of the prophets."
7634,"(7634) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: May God curse a people who take the graves of their prophets as places of worship. (Bukhari 4371 Muslim 20)"
7635,"(7635) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, that he disliked having a mosque built over the grave."
7636,"(7636) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Qadamah, on the authority of Jisra Bint Dajjaja, who said: I prayed behind Abu a single wisp. There is no woman with me."
7637,"(7637) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, who said: The woman is a class."
7638,"(7638) Wakī’ narrated to us, Al-Mughīra ibn Abi al-Hurr al-Kindi narrated to us, on the authority of Hujr ibn Anbas al-Hadrami, who said: We went out with Ali to Nahrawan until, when we were in Babylon, the afternoon prayer had come. We said: The prayer, and he remained silent. Then we said the prayer, and he remained silent. When he came out of it, he prayed, then said: I would not pray on land that had been swallowed up by it three times."
7639,"(7639) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sharik Al-Amiri, on the authority of Abdullah Abi Al-Muhall, on the authority of Ali He disliked praying during an eclipse."
7640,"(7640) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sharik, on the authority of Ibn Abi Al-Muhall, that Ali passed by Babylon and saw a sign. He prays with it."
7641,"(7641) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Umair bin Hani’, who said: I witnessed Ibn Umar while Al-Hajjaj was besieged. Ibn al-Zubayr, and Ibn Umar’s house was between them, so he may have attended prayer with them, and he may have attended prayer with them. These"
7642,"(7642) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein were praying behind Marwan. He said: Then it was said to him: Didn’t your father pray when he returned home? He said: Then he said: No, by God, they did not add anything more to him. The prayer of the Imams"
7643,"(7643) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to pray behind the princes as long as they were."
7644,"(7644) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Hurr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It does not harm a believer if he prays behind a hypocrite, nor does it benefit him. The hypocrite is the believer’s prayer behind him."
7645,"(7645) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Habib bin Jarry, who said: I asked Abu Ja`far about praying behind the princes, and he said: Pray. With them"
7646,"(7446) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, who said: I asked Maimun about praying behind the princes, and he said: Pray. With them"
7647,"(7647) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, who said: I asked Maimun about a man and he mentioned that he is one of The Kharijites, and he said: You do not pray for him, but rather you pray for God. We used to pray behind al-Hajjaj, and he was a Haruri of Azraqi."
7648,"(7648) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah used to pray with them if they delayed beyond the time. A little while, and he believes that the sin of that is upon them."
7649,"(7649) Waki’ narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, that He was praying with the pilgrims at the gates of Canada and then he went out."
7650,"(7650) Waki’ told us, Bassam told us, he said: I asked Abu Ja’far about praying with the princes, and he said: Pray with them, for we pray. With them, Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein were hastening to pray behind Marwan. He said: I said: People claim that this is piety. He said: How would it be if Al-Hasan bin Ali insulted Marwan in his face while he was on the pulpit until he took his place?"
7651,"(7651) Wakī’ narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abi Hafsā, he said: I said to Ali bin Hussein: Indeed, Aba Hamza al-Thumali, and there was exaggeration in it, said: We do not pray behind the imams, and we do not marry except with someone who sees something like ours, so he said Ali bin Al-Hussein: Rather, we pray behind them and marry them according to the Sunnah."
7652,"(7652) Waki’ told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, he said: They used to pray behind the princes and seek reward from them."
7653,"(7653) Waki` narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Uqba al-Asadi, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Sulayman, that Abu Wa’il He was grouped with the chosen one."
7654,"(7654) Waki’ narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Muslim Abi Farwa, who said: I saw Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla. He indicated to Muhammad bin Saad, while Al-Hajjaj was giving the sermon, that he should be silent."
7655,"(7655) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Mukhaymara, that he used to pray behind Al-Hajjaj."
7656,"(7656) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Yahya bin Ammar al-Mazini, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The entire earth is a mosque except the graveyard and the bathroom. (Tirmidhi 317. Abu Dawud 96)"
7657,"(7657) Hafs told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, who said: Omar saw me praying to a grave, so he started saying, O Anas the grave, So I started raising my head to look at the moon, and they said: It is only the grave that speaks."
7658,"(7658) Waki’ told us, Sufyan told us, Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: Omar saw me praying, and he said: The grave. Imam you have finished me."
7659,"(7659) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: Do not pray to the courtyard, nor to the A bathroom, not even a graveyard."
7660,"(7660) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Al-Hasan Al-Arni, who said: The entire earth is mosques except the courtyard and the bathrooms. And the cemetery."
7661,"(7661) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of his father and Khaythami, who said: He should not pray against a wall. A bathroom, not in the middle of a graveyard."
7662,"(7662) Wakī’ narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Anas, who said: He disliked that a mosque be built between Graves"
7663,"(7663) Waki’ told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: When they went out with his funeral, it attended Prayer: Stay away from the graves."
7664,"(7664) Waki` narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to recite it for three verses. For the kiss: the courtyard, the graveyard, and the bathroom."
7665,"(7665) Waki` narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Bakr ibn Qays, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he disliked praying to the oven. And he said: A house of fire."
7666,"(7666) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, disliked the prayer between Graves"
7667,"(7667) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who is overtaken by prayer in the graves, he said: He prays, and Ibn Sirin said: He returns."
7668,"(7668) Hatim bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, that he used to dislike praying in graveyards."
7669,"(7669) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Anas, that he disliked having the funeral prayer performed in The cemetery"
7670,"(7670) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Shayban, who said: I saw Musa bin Anas praying the afternoon prayer in... The grave of his brother An-Nadr bin Anas, and he was buried in the middle of the grave."
7671,"(7671) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: Ali said: Do not pray in the face of a toilet, or a bathroom, or Cemetery"
7672,"(7672) Waki’ narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, on the authority of Abu Al-Muthanna Al-Homsi, on the authority of Abi Abi Ibn Imra’, Ubadah ibn al-Samit, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is There will be leaders over you, and things will distract them from the prayer until they delay it beyond its time, so pray it at its time, so he said Man: O Messenger of God, if I meet you with them, should I pray with them? He said: Yes, if you wish. (Abu Dawud 434, Ahmad 5/315)"
7673,"(7673) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad and Alqamiya, they said: Abdullah said: It is There will be over you princes who will delay the prayer beyond its appointed time and suffocate it to the point of death. When you see them, they will do so. That is why pray in your homes, then make your prayer a glorification of praise."
7674,"(7674) Wakī’ narrated to us, Shu’bā’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Imran al-Juniyy, on the authority of Abdullah bin al-Samit, on the authority of Abu Dharr, who said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Pray the prayer at its appointed time. (Ahmad 5/157, Tayalisi 449)"
7675,"(7675) Waki’ narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, he said: I saw Ibrahim and Khaythamiya praying the noon prayer. And the afternoon prayer in their homes, then the pilgrims come and pray with him."
7676,"(7676) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, who said: I was sitting with Masruq, and Abu Ubaidah was in The mosque was in a long period of time, so when noon time came, they stood up and prayed, then they sat until when the muezzin called the call to prayer and the imam came out, they stood up. So they prayed and did it in the afternoon prayer."
7677,"(7677) Waki’ told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Hashim, that Al-Hajjaj delayed the prayer, so Abu Wa’il nodded and said: Sitting"
7678,"(7678) Waki` narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman, on the authority of Ali al-Azdi, who said: The pilgrims delayed the prayer. With his knowledge, Ibn Umar prayed while he was riding, and then people stopped and said: So Al-Hajjaj ordered him to be stabbed with him."
7679,"(7679) Waki’ narrated to us, Al-Mas’udi narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, who said: Abu Ubaidah was waiting Maghrib, and if they delay it, he unties his pack and goes out."
7680,"(7680) Waki’ told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Aamir ibn Shaqiq, who said: Al-Hajjaj used to delay the prayer on Friday prayers. Abu Wael used to order us to pray in our homes, then go to the mosque."
7681,"(7681) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu Imran al-Juniy, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Samit, on the authority of Abu Dharr, He said: My friend, may God bless him and grant him peace, advised me to perform the prayer at its appointed time. If you realize that the people have prayed, you will be You have completed your prayer, otherwise it is voluntary. (Muslim 448)"
7682,"(7682) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Ismail, who said: I saw Ata’ and Sa’id bin Jubayr and others. The newborn led the prayer, so they nodded at the time of prayer, then they sat until they prayed that prayer with him. I saw them do that many times."
7683,"(7683) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He disliked praying in our emotions. (Abu Dawud 371, Tirmidhi 600)"
7684,"(7684) Azhar told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Amr bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Do not pray with women’s hair.
Abu Bakr said: He means our clothes."
7685,"(7685) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm for a man to pray in women’s blankets."
7686,"(7686) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Hanzali, on the authority of Tawus, who said: There is no harm for a man to pray in a garment. The woman"
7687,"(7687) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Umair bin Yarim Abi Hilal, who said: I heard Ibn Al-Abbas He says: No. He says: We have departed from the prayer, for some people departed and God turned their hearts to them. Rather, they said: The prayer has been completed."
7688,"(7688) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he did not see any harm in that."
7689,"(7689) Affan narrated to us, Sa’id bin Zaid narrated to us, he said: Al-Zubayr bin Al-Kharit narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Umar. He said: It cannot be said: We have finished the prayer, but the prayer has been completed."
7690,"(7690) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Omar’s wife used to recite the Shahada. She performed the morning and evening prayers in congregation in the mosque, and she was told: Why did you go out when you knew that Omar hated that? And he gets jealous? She said: What prevented him from cursing me? They said: What prevented him was the saying of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Do not prevent God’s female servants. The mosques of God (Bukhari 9000, Ahmad 2/7)"
7691,"(7691) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Do not prevent God’s female servants from the places of God, and let them go out when they come out emptied. (Abu Dawud 566. Ahmad 438)"
7692,"(7692) Abu Khaled and Abdou bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, who said: If The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, realized what women had done today, preventing them from entering the mosques just as the women of the children of Israel prevented them. She said: I said: And we prevented him? She said: Yes. (Muslim 144 Mu’ta 15)"
7693,"(7693) Abdullah told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not prevent the female servants of God from the mosques of God. (Bukhari 9000, Abu Dawud 567)"
7694,"(7694) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Shabak, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abu Masoud’s wife used to pray the evening prayer. The last one is in the congregational mosque."
7695,"(7695) Wakī’ narrated to us, Hanzalī al-Jumahi narrated to us, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: When your women ask permission to go to the mosques, give them permission. (Bukhari 8651 Muslim 137)"
7696,"(7696) Waki` narrated to us, Mis``ar narrated to us, on the authority of Salama bin Kulayl, on the authority of Abu Amr al-Shaybani, he said: Abd said: God: No woman has ever prayed a prayer better than the prayer she prays in her home, unless she prays at the Sacred Mosque, except Old in its place, meaning its hidden."
7697,"(7697) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, that a woman asked him about praying in the mosque on Friday? He said: Your prayer in your room is better than your prayer in your house, and your prayer in your house is better than your prayer in Your room, and your prayer in your room is better than your prayer in the mosque of your people."
7698,"(7698) Waki’ narrated to us, Sulaiman bin Al-Mughirah narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, he said: He said: Abdullah: A woman is naked, and the closest thing she is to her Lord is when she is in the depths of her house, then when she goes out, look at her. Satan"
7699,"(7699) Waki` narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Farwa al-Hamdani, on the authority of Abu Amr al-Shaybani, he said: I saw Ibn Masoud counting the women and taking them out of the mosque on Friday."
7700,"(7700) Wakī’ narrated to us, Iyas ibn Daghfāl narrated to us, he said: Al-Hasan was asked about a woman who had been appointed to her duty if her husband was taken away. It is a form of imprisonment to pray in every mosque in which the prayer in Basra is combined into two rak’ahs. Al-Hasan said: You pray in a mosque. Her people, for she cannot bear it. If Omar ibn al-Khattab overtook her, it would make her head hurt."
7701,"(7701) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Masruq, on the authority of Abu Amr Al-Shaybani, who said: I heard the Lord of this house, That is to say, Ibn Masoud swore an oath and took the oath solemnly: No woman has prayed a prayer more beloved to God than a prayer in her home, except during Hajj. Or a woman, except for a woman who has lost her way from among the beasts."
7702,"(7702) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, Ibn Lahiyya narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn al-Mundhir al-Sa’i narrated to me, on the authority of his father On the authority of her grandmother, Umm Humaid, she said: I said: O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, our husbands prevent us from praying with you. We love to pray with you. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Your prayer in your homes is better than your prayer in Your quarantine, and your prayer in your quarantine is better than your prayer in congregation. (Tabarani 3561, Ahmad 6/371)"
7703,"(7703) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abraham, who said: Abraham had three wives, but he did not leave them. They go out to a group, but not a group."
7704,"(7704) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: The best rows of women are the last ones and the worst ones are the front ones."
7705,"(7705) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah used to say: The best of the rows. The late women."
7706,"(7706) Ali bin Musahir told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Zur’a, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The best of the women's rows is the last and the worst is the first."
7707,"(7707) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: It used to be said: The best rows of women are the back ones and the worst ones. Introduction"
7708,"(7708) Abdă bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, similar to this."
7709,"(7709) Hushaym told us, he said: Husayn told us, he said: It was told that Ibn Masoud used to present the old women in the classroom. The first of the women's rows, and the young men last to the back of the row."
7710,"(7710) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, Zuhair bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: The best rows Delayed women and their upfront evil."
7711,"(7711) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: The best rows for men are the front and the worst are the back, and the best rows for women are the last and the worst are the front. (Tirmidhi 224, Abu Dawud 678)"
7712,"(7712) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father Hariri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The best rows of men are the first ones, and the worst rows of men are the last ones, and the best The women's rows are the last ones, and the worst of the women's rows are the first ones. (Hamidi 1001, Ahmad 2/340)"
7713,"(7713) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, he said: Thabit bin Aslam told us, he said: Salah bin told us Ashim, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Whoever prays two rak’ahs does not talk to himself during them at all. He did not ask God for anything but He gave it to him."
7714,"(7714) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, Laith narrated to us, on the authority of Issa, on the authority of Zayd bin Arta, on the authority of Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What is given to a servant in this world is better for him than that he be given permission to enter it. Two rak'ahs and he prays them. (Tirmidhi 2911. Ahmad 5/268)"
7715,"(7715) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Malik, on the authority of Abu Hazim, who said: I passed with Abu Hurairah over a grave that had recently been buried, He said: Two light rak'ahs of what you despise. This additional rak'ah is more beloved to him than the rest of your world."
7716,"(7716) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: A man bought a wall in Medina and made a profit from it. One hundred perfect palm trees. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Shall I not inform you of something better than this? A man performed ablution and performed it well, then prayed two rak'ahs in a cave or at the foot of a mountain."
7717,"(7717) Waki` narrated to us, some of our companions narrated to us, on the authority of al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu al-Ward, on the authority of Ka`b: Indeed, in this To inform a worshiping people, he said: The five daily prayers."
7718,"(7718) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Khaled, Mas’ar, and Al-Bakhtari bin Al-Mukhtar narrated to us, they heard it from Abu Bakr. Ibn Ammarah Ibn Ruwaybah Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of his father, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: He will not enter. Hellfire is the one who prayed before the sunrise and before it set, and a man from the people of Basra said to him: You heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes, I bear witness that I heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. My ears heard it and my heart understood it. (Muslim 213. Ahmad 4/261)"
7719,"(7719) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, who said: We were showing the Qur’an to Abdullah, and a man from Thaqif asked him, He said: O Abu Abdul Rahman, which deeds are best? He said: Prayer, and whoever does not pray has no debt."
7720,"(7720) Husayn bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Masruq, who said: There is no better case. That the servant should be answered in it, unless he is in the path of God, rather than being helpless, with his face prostrating."
7721,"(7721) Husayn bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Harith, he said: It was narrated that it was stolen. He used to say: Whoever memorizes these prayers will not be counted as one of the heedless, for in his negligence he will be destroyed."
7722,"(7722) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Ismail, on the authority of the stronghold of Al-Khathami, on the authority of Ali, who said: Who did not He prays, but he has disbelieved."
7723,"(7723) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Imran bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Ali bin Thabit, who said: The offering of the pious is prayer."
7724,"(7724) Waki’ narrated to us, Mis’ar and Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Mughirah Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Ali bin Rabi’ah. Al-Walbiy, on the authority of Asmaa bin Al-Hakam Al-Fazari, on the authority of Ali, who said: Whenever I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, A hadith that God benefited me with as He wished of it. If someone else narrated it to me, I made him swear to him, and if he swore to me, I told him the truth, and indeed he refused. Bakr told me, and Abu Bakr told the truth, that he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: There is no man who commits a sin and performs ablution. So he performs ablution well. Sufyan said: Then he prays two rak’ahs. Mas’ar said: Then he prays and asks forgiveness from God, unless He forgives him. (Tirmidhi 3006. Abu Dawud 1516)"
7725,"(7725) Waki’ narrated to us, Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Misra and Al-Mughirah bin Shibl, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, On the authority of Salman, he said: The five daily prayers are expiations for what is between them as long as you avoid killing."
7726,"(7726) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, who said: Abdullah said: True prayers are expiations for what Between them as long as major sins are avoided. (Tabarani 8740)"
7727,"(7727) Waki’ narrated to us, Hisham bin Urwah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hamran bin Aban, on the authority of Uthman bin Affan, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no man who performs ablution and performs it well, then prays except that his sins will be forgiven. Between it and the other prayer. (Muslim 206)"
7728,"(7728) Zayd bin Harun told us, Awf and Al-Jariri told us, on the authority of Qasamah bin Zuhair, on the authority of Abu Musa, He said: The example of the five daily prayers is like a flowing river at the door of one of you, and he bathes in it five times every day. So what are they left with after that? On him from his family."
7729,"(7729) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Ali ibn Ata’, who said: I heard Ibrahim ibn Yuhannis, on the authority of Abu Darda’ He said: The example of the five daily prayers is that of a man at his door with a river in which he bathes five times every day. So what remains of that? tuberculosis"
7730,"(7730) Waki’ narrated to us, Mas’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sakhrah Jami’ bin Shaddad, who said: I heard Hamran bin Aban Mawla. Othman says: I used to add water to Othman, and not a day came when he did not spill a drop of water on him. Othman said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told us when we finished this prayer. Mas’ar said: I see him. He said: afternoon, and he said: I do not know whether I should speak to you, or whether I should remain silent. He said: We said, O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, if it is good. So tell us, and if it is other than that, then God and His Messenger know best. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no man He performs ablution and performs it well, then prays, except that what came between him and the other prayer will be forgiven."
7731,"(7731) Waki’ narrated to us, Al-Awza’i narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul-Wahid bin Qays, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The expiation of all Two rak'ahs."
7732,"(7732) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And he said: The example of the five daily prayers is like a flowing river full of water at the door of one of you, from which he bathes five times every day. He said: So he said: Al-Hassan: What remains of this form of tuberculosis? (Muslim 284, Bayhaqi 63)"
7733,"(7733) Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: The example of the five daily prayers is like a flowing river at the door of one of you, in which he bathes five times every day. What remains of his life? (Ahmad 2/441)"
7734,"(7734) Waki’ narrated to us, Mis’ar and Shu’ba narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Barda, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Ibn Omar says: I have not prayed a prayer except with the hope that it would be an expiation for what was before me."
7735,"(7735) Waki’ told us, Mis’ar told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, he said: Abdullah said: They will be burned when they pray. She washed the noon prayer, then they were burned, so when they prayed the afternoon prayer, she was washed, then they were burned, so when they prayed the sunset prayer, she was washed until he mentioned All prayers."
7736,"(7736) Waki’ narrated to us, Al-Masoudi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Laqit bin Qubaysa Al-Jaafari. A man from Abdullah’s companions said: There was Abdullah, so he mentioned something similar to him."
7737,"(7737) Waki’ narrated to us, Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: The example of the five daily prayers is like a flowing river at the door of one of you, from which he bathes five times every day, so what? Stay away from tuberculosis?"
7738,"(7738) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Hani’ ibn Uthman narrated to us, on the authority of his mother, Humiz, son of Yasir, on the authority of Her grandmother, Yusira, who was one of the female emigrants, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: May you be With recitation, glorification, and greatness, and hold them together with your fingertips. Indeed, on the Day of Resurrection, they will be brought to each other with clear parts. And do not be negligent and forget mercy. (Tirmidhi 3583. Ahmad 6/370)"
7739,"(7739) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Tamimah, on the authority of a woman from Banu Kulayb. She said: Aisha saw me reciting the tasbih with rosaries with me, so she said: Where are the evidence? It means fingers."
7740,"(7740) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hakim bin Daylam, on the authority of a servant of Sa’d: That Sa’d He used to glorify God with pebbles and stones."
7741,"(7741) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hakim Ibn al-Daylam, on the authority of Sa’d’s servant: that Sa’d was He glorifies pebbles and stones."
7742,"(7742) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Al-Akhnas, he said: A servant of Abi Saeed narrated to me, on the authority of my father. Saeed: He used to take three pebbles and place them on his thigh and say the tasbih. He would place one, then say the tasbih. He put down another, then he said the tasbih and put down another, then raised it and did the same, and said: Do not say the tasbih while whistling."
7743,"(7743) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadhru, on the authority of a man from Al-Taffawa, who said: It was revealed to my father. He saw a bird with him a bag containing pebbles, or a stone, and he would say, Glory be to God, Glory be to God, until when what was in the bag ran out, he would throw it in. To a black maid, so she collected him, then gave him to her."
7744,"(7744) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Musa Al-Qari, on the authority of Talha bin Abdullah, on the authority of Zazan, he said: I took From Umm Ya’fur, praises to her. When I came to Ali, he taught me, and said: O Abu Umar, repeat her praises to Umm Ya’fur."
7745,"(7745) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: I saw The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, tied the knot with his hand, meaning praise. (Tirmidhi 3411, Abu Dawud 1427)"
7746,"(7746) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, that he saw no harm in a man reciting the tasbeeh and tying the knot. Glory be to Him"
7747,"(7747) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Mukhtar bin Saad, who said: I saw Muhammad bin Ali reciting the voluntary tasbih and performing voluntary prayers. With his hand"
7748,"(7748) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, the muezzin of Banu Hanifi, who said: I saw what the Hanafi made and he commanded it. Al-Hajjaj asked him to be crucified at his door, and I looked at him and he was on the tree and he was glorifying, glorifying, glorifying, praising God and praising Him. By God, until he reached the age of twenty-nine, he tied knots in his hand, and he was stabbed in that state. I saw him tied up a month later. Twenty-nine in his hand, and he could see a light at night."
7749,"(7749) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah disliked the number and said: He is more secure. May God bless him with his good deeds?"
7750,"(7750) Azhar al-Samman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Uqba, who said: I asked Ibn Umar about a man who mentions God and makes a marriage contract? He said: Do they call God to account?"
7751,"(7751) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Waqa’i, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, who said: Omar ibn al-Khattab saw a man praising God. With his praises, Omar said: The only sufficient part of that is to say: Glory be to God, He has filled the heavens and the earth, and He has filled whatever He wills with anything. After, and he says: Praise be to God, He has filled the heavens and the earth, and He has filled whatever He wills with anything. After, and He says: God is Great, He has filled the heavens and the earth. And He filled it with whatever He wanted after that."
7752,"(7752) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim: It was He forbade his daughter to help women in unwinding the threads of praise with which he used to recite the tasbih."
7753,"Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Yunus told us, he said: Baqi bin Mukhlid told us, may God have mercy on him, he said: Abu Bakr told us, he said:
(7753) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yusuf, that Al-Sa’ib informed him: Omar gathered the people against Ubayy. And Tamim, they used to perform eleven rak’ah prayers, reciting the Qur’an in the hundred, meaning in Ramadan."
7754,"(7754) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: Omar called the reciters in Ramadan and ordered the fastest among them. Reciting is to recite thirty verses, the middle is twenty-five verses, and the slow is twenty verses."
7755,"(7755) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ali ibn al-Aqmar: that Masruq recited while standing in two rak’ahs. With a spider."
7756,"(7756) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Nafi’ ibn Umar, who said: I heard Ibn Abi Mulkiah say: I used to stand in charge of the people. The month of Ramadan, so I recite in the rak’ah: {Praise be to God, the Breaker} and the like, and it has not informed me that anyone does that independently."
7757,"(7757) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Waqa’i, who said: Sa’id bin Jubayr used to recite five times in every rak’ah. And twenty verses."
7758,"(7758) Hammad bin Khaled told us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of his father, who said: Omar bin Abdul-Aziz was the commander of those They recite ten verses in Ramadan, ten verses in each rak'ah."
7759,"(7759) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, who said: Abu Majlaz used to perform prayers in the neighborhood during Ramadan. He concludes every seventh."
7760,"(7760) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Araak bin Malik, on the authority of his father, who said: I have realized the people in During the month of Ramadan, ropes are tied for them, and they will hold on to them for the duration of the night’s prayers."
7761,"(7761) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Whoever leads the people in Ramadan, let him take With ease, if he was slow to recite, then he should complete the Qur’an completely, and if he was slow in reciting, then he should complete it. And a half, and if he reads quickly, then twice."
7762,"(7762) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Qais, on the authority of Shutair ibn Shikal: He used to pray twenty rak'ahs and the Witr prayer in Ramadan."
7763,"(7763) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Amr bin Qays, on the authority of Abu al-Hasana’: that Ali commanded a man He prays twenty rak'ahs with them in Ramadan."
7764,"(7764) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa’id, that Omar ibn al-Khattab ordered a man to pray They have twenty rak'ahs."
7765,"(7765) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Umar, who said: Ibn Abi Malikay used to lead us in prayer on the twenty twentieth of Ramadan. raka’ah and reciting “Praise be to the angels” in raka’ah."
7766,"(7766) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, who said: Ubayy bin Ka’b was He leads the people in prayer during Ramadan in Medina with twenty rak'ahs and prays Witr with three rak'ahs."
7767,"(7767) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith: He used to lead the people in prayer during Ramadan. At night, he performs twenty rak’ahs, and he performs Witr with three rak’ahs and Qunoot before bowing."
7768,"(7768) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Khalaf, on the authority of Rabi’, and he praised him well, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari: He used to pray five Taraweeh prayers in Ramadan and pray Witr three times."
7769,"(7769) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, who said: Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Aswad used to lead us in prayer during Ramadan. Forty rak'ahs and the Witr prayer with seven."
7770,"(7770) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdul Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I overtook the people while they were praying twenty-three days. Rakaa with the Witr."
7771,"(7771) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Qays, who said: I met the people in Medina in the time of Omar bin Abd. Al-Aziz and Aban bin Uthman pray thirty-six rak’ahs and pray Witr with three."
7772,"(7772) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Ubaid: That Ali bin Rabi’i used to lead them in prayer in Ramadan consists of five taraweehs and the Witr prayer with three."
7773,"(7773) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Waqa’i, who said: Sa’id bin Jubayr used to lead us in Ramadan and lead us in prayer. Twenty nights are six Tarwihs, and if it is the last ten, he secludes himself in the mosque and prays seven Tarwihs with us."
7774,"(7774) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Uthman informed us, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas. : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray twenty rak’ahs and the Witr prayer in Ramadan. (Abdullah bin Hamid 653)"
7775,"(7775) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zaid bin Wahhab, who said: Abdullah used to lead us in faith. Ramadan."
7776,"(7776) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash narrated to us, saying: I asked Ata’ whether Ali would lead them in prayer during Ramadan? He said: The best companions of Ali Zazan, Abu Al-Bakhtari and others used to invite their families and believe in the mosque. In Ramadan."
7777,"(7777) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdul Rahman Al-Jurshi, on the authority of Jubayr Ibn Nufayr Al-Hadrami, on the authority of Abu Dharr, said: We fasted with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during Ramadan, but he did not even lead us in prayer. Seven days of the month remained, so he stayed with us until a third of the night had passed, then he did not stay with us on the sixth, then he stayed with us on the fifth. Until half of the night had passed, we said: O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, if you stayed with us, we would stay for the rest of this night. He said: Whoever stands with the imam until he finishes, it will be recorded for him to have spent the night standing in prayer. He said: Then he led us in prayer until three days of the month remained, then he led us in prayer and gathered his family and wives. He said: So he stood until we became afraid. That we should miss Al-Falah. He said: I said: What is Al-Falah? He said: Suhoor. (Abu Dawud 1730, Ahmad 5/163)"
7778,"(7778) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Muawiyah ibn Salih, he said: Na’im ibn Ziyad Abu Talha al-Anmari narrated to me, He said: I heard Al-Numan bin Bashir on the pulpit of Homs saying: We stood with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for three nights. And we stayed with him for the night from twenty-fifth to half the night, and we stayed with him for the night. On the twenty-seventh, until we thought we would miss the day of Falah, but we were counting it as suhoor. (Ahmad 4/272, Ibn Khuzaymah 2204)"
7779,"(7779) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Talha bin Yazid, on the authority of Hudhayfah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led us up one night during Ramadan in a chamber made of palm leaves. Then he poured a bucket of water on him, then said: God is the Greatest, the Possessor of kingdom, might, pride, and greatness."
7780,"(7780) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He wanted to observe Ramadan without any resolve. (Tirmidhi 808, Abu Dawud 1366)"
7781,"(7781) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah: That the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose during Ramadan some He was praying and they followed his voice, but when he learned of them he lowered his voice."
7782,"(7782) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, who said: Abdullah used to lead us in prayer during Ramadan. And he departs with a night over him."
7783,"(7783) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ali: He led them in Ramadan."
7784,"(7784) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Ali, on the authority of his father, he said: Suwayd bin Ghafla used to lead us in prayer. He will join us in the month of Ramadan when he is twenty-one hundred years old."
7785,"(7785) Shababah narrated to us, he said: Laith bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abd. Al-Qari, he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab went out during the month of Ramadan while the people were definitely praying, so he said: If we had gathered all of them against Qari. One person would have been better, so he would have gathered them together against Ubayy ibn Ka’b."
7786,"(7786) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salama: That the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He desires to perform Ramadan without ordering it with his resolve."
7787,"(7787) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Nasr ibn Ali, on the authority of Nadr ibn Shayban, who said: I asked Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, So he mentioned on the authority of his father. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God has made fasting obligatory upon you and has established laws for you. His resurrection, so whoever fasts out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven. (Ahmad 1/194, Tayalisi 224)"
7788,"(7788) Waki’ told us, saying: Hisham bin Urwah told us, on the authority of his father: Omar bin Al-Khattab ordered his father to pray. With people during the month of Ramadan."
7789,"(7789) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Misra, on the authority of Tawus, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: Omar called me. To have lunch with him. Abu Bakr said: He means the suhoor meal in Ramadan. He heard the people shouting when they left the mosque. He said: What Yes? He said: The people gathered around you wherever they left the mosque. He said: What remains of the night is better than what has passed."
7790,"(7790) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abd al-Qari, who said: Omar said: In The hour in which they sleep is more wondrous to me than the hour in which they stand."
7791,"(7791) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Yazid al-Madini, he said: Ibn Abbas said regarding the standing Ramadan: What they leave behind is better than what they stay in it."
7792,"(7792) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Mu’tamir, he said: I asked Al-Hasan which hour should I go to? He said: See how attached this person is to the people."
7793,"(7793) Wakī’ told us, he said: Shu’bā told us, on the authority of Al-Hikam. He said: They used to sleep like that before rising in the month of Ramadan. Ramadan."
7794,"(7794) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Usama bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Araj, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib, he said: Omar said: You You call upon the best of the night for its last."
7795,"(7795) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Mis`ar narrated to us, on the authority of Habib, who said: A man said: The night had passed, and he said: The lifespan of what remains of The night is better than what it passed."
7796,"(7796) Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he did not stand up with the people. During the month of Ramadan, he said: Salem and Al-Qasim did not stay with the people."
7797,"(7797) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: A man asked Ibn Umar whether I should stand behind the imam in the month of Ramadan. Ramadan, and he said: Listen as if you were a donkey."
7798,"(7798) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If only I had had a surah with me. Or two surahs, because I repeat them as much as I love rather than standing behind the imam during the month of Ramadan."
7799,"(7799) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: Abraham used to lead them in what was written, and he did not He leads them in the Ramadan prayer, Al-Alqamah and Al-Aswad."
7800,"(7800) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: Ibrahim and Alqamah did not stand with the people during Ramadan."
7801,"(7801) Qattan bin Abdullah Abu Murri told us, on the authority of Nasr al-Muallem, he said: Omar bin Uthman told me, he said: I asked Al-Hasan So I said: O Abu Saeed, Ramadan comes, or Ramadan approaches, and the people stand up in the mosques, so what do you think? Should I stand up with the people or Should I pray for myself? He said: It is more beloved to me that you recite the Qur’an than that it be recited to you."
7802,"(7802) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abbad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Sa’ib, he said: I was leading the people in prayer during Ramadan, and while I was praying I heard Omar saying “Allahu Akbar” at the door of the mosque. He came and performed Umrah and entered my classroom. Behind you"
7803,"(7803) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus: He used to pray with them during the month of Ramadan. He prays for himself and kneels and prostrates with them."
7804,"(7804) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad: He used to choose to stand with the people during the month of Ramadan. Ramadan."
7805,"(7805) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The Mujtahids used to pray next to the mosque. The imam leads the people in prayer during the month of Ramadan."
7806,"(7806) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, who said: I saw Abdullah bin Abi Mulki leading the people in prayer. Ramadan is behind the Maqam, with those who prayed behind it, and the people after that in the rest of the mosque, from those around the House to those praying."
7807,"(7807) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ash’ath ibn Abi Al-Sha’athi, who said: I witnessed Mecca in the time of Ibn Al-Zubayr is in Ramadan, and the imam is leading one group of people in prayer alone, and the people are praying in the vicinity of the mosque."
7808,"(7808) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, who said: I saw Shabath bin Rabi’i. And people with him prayed alone in Ramadan, and the people were in prayer, and I saw Shabath praying alone in a veil."
7809,"(7809) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The Imam used to lead the people in prayer in the mosque. Those who are Mujtahid pray in the vicinity of the mosque for themselves."
7810,"(7810) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn Jubayr and Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who stands between the two tarawihs and recites until the imam gets up and enters with him. His people said: He hated one of them. And the others did not hate it.
 Hisham said: He is Yunus bin Jubayr."
7811,"(7811) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Harun ibn Abi Maryam, on the authority of Ibn al-Aswad: He used to lead forty people in prayer with them. rak'ah, and perform Witr with them, and pray twelve rak'ahs between the two Tarawihs, and say between the two Tarawihs: Salat."
7812,"(7812) Affan told us, he said: Hammam told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told us, that a man from the people of Syria It is said that Abu Sufyan told him that Buhayr bin Raysan told him that he was with Ubadah bin Al-Samit and witnessed this. He rebuked them from praying when the imam departed during Ramadan, and he began to rebuke them while they did not care or stop, so he struck them. I saw him beating them for that."
7813,"(7813) Yahya bin Wadhih Abu Tamila told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Amri, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Jubayr, he used to hate saying the prayer between the two Tarwihs."
7814,"(7814) Abbad bin Awwam narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders and Al-Hasan: They both hated to comment during Ramadan."
7815,"(7815) Abbad told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, who said: There is no harm in him. They will only return to something better, in which they hope. And they are acquitted of the evil they fear."
7816,"(7816) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Rabi’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he saw the recitation during the month of Ramadan, and Al-Hasan said, “No.” You bore people."
7817,"(7817) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Amr, that he prayed behind Abu Hurairah in Ramadan. He used to pray two rak'ahs, then say the salaam, then stand up and pray two rak'ahs."
7818,"(7818) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Yahya bin Wathhab, that he used to lead them in prayer during the month of Ramadan. Standing and he did not say the salutation except in four rak’ahs."
7819,"(7819) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, who said: Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Aswad used to lead us in prayer on the Night of Fitr."
7820,"(7820) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Omar bin Ayyub informed me, he said: They informed me. Abu Iyas Muawiyah ibn Qurayh said: I was staying with Amr ibn al-Nu`man ibn Muqrin, and when Ramadan came, a man came to me. Two thousand dirhams from Musab bin Al-Zubayr, and he said: The prince congratulates you and says: We have not called an honorable reader unless he has A favor has come to him from us, so seek help from these two at the expense of this partner of yours. Amr said: Convey your greetings to the prince and say: By God, we do not recite the Qur’an with the intention of this world and to return it to Him."
7821,"(7821) Waki` narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Maqil: That he led the people in prayer in The month of Ramadan, and when it was the Day of Fitr, he sent to Ubayd Allah ibn Ziyad with jewelry and five hundred dirhams, and he returned them and said: We do not take any reward for the Qur’an."
7822,"(7822) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Masoudi told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, he said: No reward is taken for the Qur’an."
7823,"(7823) Jarir told us, on the authority of a man: that Sa’id bin Jubayr led the people in Ramadan, and the pilgrims were sent to him with a robe. So he accepted it."
7824,"(7824) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Waqid, on the authority of Zazan, he said, I heard him say: Whoever reads the Qur’an It will be said that he will come on the Day of Resurrection and his face will be bone with no flesh on it."
7825,"(7825) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hisham al-Dastawai narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Rashid, On the authority of Abdullah bin Shibl, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Read the Qur’an, and do not eat from it, nor Take it abundantly, do not abstain from it, and do not abuse it to excess. (Ahmad 3/444, Abu Ali 1515)"
7826,"(7826) Waki’ told us, he said: Zaid bin Al-Hatim told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, Omar said: Recite the Qur’an and ask God for it. Before people read it, they will ask people about it."
7827,"(7827) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Abd al-A’la, on the authority of Suwayd ibn Ghafla: He forbade praying on the road."
7828,"(7828) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Sayyar bin Ma’rur, who said: Omar saw people praying on the road, so he said: Pray. In the mosque."
7829,"(7829) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Do not pray on a road horse, and do not dismount on it, for it is a haven for serpents and wild beasts. (Ahmad 3/382 and Abd al-Razzaq 9247)"
7830,"(7830) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit al-Bunani, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: They were companions of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed in the highways of Ahwaz, and Anas bin Malik used to pray in the corridor of his servants."
7831,"(7831) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, on the authority of Hudhayfy, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: The entire earth has been made a mosque for us."
7832,"(7832) Hushaym told us, he said: Sayyar told us, he said: Zaid al-Faqir told us, he said: Jabir bin Abdullah told us. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The earth has been made for you a sanctuary and a mosque. Whichever man from your nation has attained it? Prayer, let him pray wherever you reach him. (Bukhari 335. Muslim 2)"
7833,"(7833) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Mujahid and Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The earth has been made for me a purification and a mosque. (Bukhari 2152. Ahmad 1/301)"
7834,"(7834) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of his father, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: The earth has been made for me a purification and a mosque. (Ahmad 4/416)"
7835,"(7835) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymimi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Dhar, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: Wherever prayer leads you, pray, it is a mosque. (Bukhari 3366, Muslim 370, Ahmad 5/160)"
7836,"(7836) Waki’ told us, he said: Omar bin Dhar told us, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Dhar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And peace be upon him: The earth has been made for me a place of mosque and purification. (Tayalisi 472. Ahmad 5/161)"
7837,"(7837) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Harith, on the authority of his father, who said: We were with Abu Musa in a house. So the time for prayer came and he led us in prayer on dung and straw, so we said, “Will you lead us in prayer here while the desert is next to you?” He said: The wilderness and here are the same."
7838,"(7838) Waki’ told us, he said: Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, he said: I saw Salim sweeping a place, then he prayed in it."
7839,"(7839) Malik bin Ismail told us, he said: Mandal told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, on the authority of Abu Dharr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The earth has been made for me a purification and a mosque. (Abu Dawud 490)"
7840,"(7840) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: The people used to recite the Qur’an frequently during Ramadan, every reader. Following the example of his friend, Omar ibn Abd al-Aziz took over and said: Let every reciter read from wherever he likes."
7841,"(7841) Hushaym told us, he said: Abd al-Malik bin Umair told us, he said: Jabir bin Samarra told us: Some people complained Saad went to Omar ibn al-Khattab, he said, and he complained about the prayer, he said: Then Omar wrote to him, and he came to him, he said: So he mentioned what He complained about it, and he mentioned that they complained about the prayer, so Saad said: I will pray with them the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him. Indeed, I adhere to them in the first two verses and omit them in the last two verses. He said: That is the suspicion of you, O father. Isaac (Bukhari 7700, Muslim 159)"
7842,"(7842) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Bishr al-Hujaimi, on the authority of Abu al-Siddiq, on the authority of Abu Sa`id, He said: We were anticipating the resurrection of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at noon and afternoon, so we were anticipating his resurrection at noon. The first two rak'ahs were as long as thirty verses, and we estimated that his standing in the other two rak'ahs was half of that. We mourned his standing in the first two rak'ahs of the afternoon prayer, as much as the other two rak'ahs of the noon prayer. The other two rak'ahs of the afternoon prayer are half of that."
7843,"(7843) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham Al-Dastawai, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite with us in the first two rak’ahs. From noon, and he would sometimes make us hear verses, and he would lengthen the first and shorten the second, and he would do that in prayer. The first rak'ah of the afternoon prayer is prolonged and shortened during the second, and it was recited for us in the first two rak'ahs of the afternoon prayer."
7844,"(7844) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Abu Uthman: That Omar used to pray the noon prayer at noon. He prolongs the first rak’ah."
7845,"(7845) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Abi Bakr, who said: I prayed behind Al-Qasim, and he used to prolong the first two prayers. Taller than the other two. The first two are from Dhahr, the first two are from Asr, the first two are from Morocco, and the first two are from Asr. Dinner"
7846,"(7846) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Bakr, who said: I prayed behind Salim, and he used to do the same thing. Omar bin Abdul Aziz used to do that."
7847,"(7847) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, who said: I saw Omar ibn Abd al-Aziz leading us in the noon prayer. He lengthens the first two verses, makes the last two verses shorter, and makes the ‘Asr time more gentle."
7848,"(7848) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Jabir, on the authority of Makhoul: That he used to prolong the first Rakaa"
7849,"(7849) Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awan narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Abi Salamah, on the authority of his father, he said: Othman bin Affan prolongs the first two rak'ahs of the noon prayer, reciting Surah Al-Baqarah during them."
7850,"(7850) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He prayed Fajr and sat in his seat until the sun rose. (Muslim 444, Abu Dawud 1288)"
7851,"(7851) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Musa bin Abdullah bin Ishaq bin Talha, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, he said: It was Talhah stands firm in his place of prayer wherever he prayed and does not leave until the Subha is brought and he recites the Subha."
7852,"(7852) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: I was informed about a man from Banu Tamim that he entered upon Al-Hasan. Ibn Ali while he was sitting in his prayer place, and he said: There is no Muslim who prays the morning prayer and then sits in his prayer place unless he wears a veil. From the fire"
7853,"(7853) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Badr, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’atha’i Al-Muharbibi, on the authority of Salman, he said: When you pray the morning prayer, remember God until the sun rises, but if you do not do that, then sleep, for the sleeper is safe."
7854,"(7854) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Ashhab, on the authority of al-Hasan: that Abu Hurairah met a man, and he said: It is as if you are not From the people of the country? He said: Yes, he said: Shall I not tell you a hadith that I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that you may benefit from it? I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: The first thing a servant will be called to account for is the prayer. If he completes it, otherwise it will be said: For the angels completed his voluntary prayer. Al-Hasan said: And all other deeds are based on that. (Bukhari 1593; Abu Ali 6197)"
7855,"(7855) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Tamim al-Dari, who said: The first The servant will not be held accountable for the prayer. If he completes it and it is said: “Watch for it if it was voluntary,” then if it was voluntary then complete it. Written from voluntary. (Ahmad 1030 Darami 1355)"
7856,"(7856) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Tamim bin Salama, who said: The first thing a servant is asked about is the His prayer, if it is accepted from him, then all of his deeds will be accepted from him, and if it is rejected, then all of his deeds will be rejected."
7857,"(7857) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, on the authority of Al-Anbari’s repentance, on the authority of Muwarriq Al-Ijlili, he said: I told Ibn Omar: Do you pray the Duha prayer? He said: No, I said: Omar’s prayer? He said: No, I said: Did Abu Bakr pray? He said: No, I said the Prophet’s prayers, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: I don't think so. (Bukhari 1175. Ahmad 2/23)"
7858,"(7858) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: I have not prayed the forenoon prayer since I converted to Islam. Except that I circumambulate the Kaaba."
7859,"(7859) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Al-Hakam Ibn Al-Araj, who said: I asked Ibn Umar about the Duha prayer, and he Leaning with his back to the lap of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: An innovation, and what a good innovation. (Bukhari 1775, Muslim 220)"
7860,"(7860) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Shu’abi narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abu Ubaydī, he said: They did not inform me. One of the people saw Ibn Masoud praying the noon prayer."
7861,"(7861) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, he said: We used to recite in the mosque. So the people would continue to recite the recitation after Ibn Masoud stood up, then we would get up and pray the noon prayer. This reached Ibn Masoud, and he said: Servants. God, why do you burden the servants of God unless God burdens them? If you must do so, then in your homes."
7862,"(7862) Waki’ told us, he said: My father and Israel told me, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Tamimi, he said: I asked Ibn Umar About the noon prayer, he said: And does the noon prayer have a prayer?"
7863,"(7863) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: It was not. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited the rosary of the morning prayer. She said: And he used to leave things that he disliked so that he could live in peace. There it is. (Ahmed 170)"
7864,"(7864) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, does not pray the Subhaha of the morning prayer, but I praise it. (Bukhari 1177 and Abu Dawud 1287)"
7865,"(7865) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, he said: He did not pray. The sacrifice"
7866,"(7866) Waki’ told us, he said: Hajib bin Omar told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Al-Araj, he said: I asked Ibn Omar about the Duha prayer? He said: Heresy."
7867,"(7867) Waki` narrated to us, he said: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abbas, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, he said: I give up the Duha prayer, and I I miss her"
7868,"(7868) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Nāṣ ibn Qaym Abu Al-Khattab narrated to us, on the authority of Shaddad Abi Ammar Al-Shami, on the authority of Abi Harry, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever adheres to the pre-emption of the sacrifice, his sins will be forgiven, even if It was like sea foam. (Ahmed 497)"
7869,"(7869) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hisham al-Dastawai narrated to us, on the authority of al-Qasim bin Awf al-Shaybani, on the authority of Zayd bin Arqam. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came out to the people of Quba’i while they were praying the pre-dhuhr prayer, and he said: The prayer of the people who come back when The chapters faded in the morning. (Muslim 144. Ahmad 4/367)"
7870,"(7870) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Khams ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Shaqiq al-Uqaylī, he said: I said: To Aisha: Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, perform the noon prayer? She said: No, unless he comes from his absence. (Muslim 761, Ahmad 6/171)"
7871,"(7871) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said : I have never seen the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, praying the noon prayer except once. (Ahmad 2/446, An-Nasa’i 477)"
7872,"(7872) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad: that Aisha used to pray the noon prayer. A long prayer."
7873,"(7873) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Abu Al-Minhal Al-Tai’i Nasr bin Aws narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zaid, on the authority of Abu Huraira, he said: He said to me: You must perform the two prostrations of the pre-dhuhr prayer, for they are better for you than two she-camels of cattle from the produce of Banu Buhtur."
7874,"(7874) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Asama bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Al-Rabab: that Abu Dharr prayed The pre-morning period was prolonged."
7875,"(7875) Ismail told us, on the authority of Habib bin Al-Shahid, who said: Ikrimah was asked about Ibn Abbas’s Duha prayer? He said: He used to lead her in prayer today and leave her ten days in prayer."
7876,"(7876) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, who said: Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab used to lead the noon prayer."
7877,"(7877) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to pray the noon prayer and make supplications."
7878,"(7878) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansur Ughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to hate that Perpetuate the Dhuha prayer like the obligatory prayer."
7879,"(7879) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, She used to close her door, then pray the noon prayer."
7880,"(7880) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malikki, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he was asked Concerning the Dhuha prayer, he said: It is in the Book of God, and no one will delve into it except a diver. Then he recited: (In houses that God has permitted to be raised And His name is mentioned therein, and He glorifies Him therein in the mornings and the evenings.)"
7881,"(7881) Waki` narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Salim al-Aftas, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr: He prayed the noon prayer in The Kaaba"
7882,"(7882) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Mutayr bin Juwayriyah, who said: I saw Al-Dahhak praying the noon prayer, and I saw Abu Majlaz prays at his home during the morning prayer."
7883,"(7883) Waki’ told us, he said: Yahya bin Muslim Al-Hamdani told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Amr Al-Qurashi, he said: Abu Abdullah bin Omar followed me so that I could learn from him, and I did not see him praying the Subha. And when he saw them praying, he would say: Who? The best of what they did is glorify them."
7884,"(7884) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Al-Awwam, on the authority of Suleiman bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He recommended My friend, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, if I pray the Dhuha prayer, it is the prayer of the returnees."
7885,"(7885) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of his paternal uncle Salama bin Simak, who said: I heard Omar bin Al-Khattab saying: Sacrifice as servants. God bless the morning prayer."
7886,"(7886) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Yusuf bin Suhayb narrated to us, on the authority of Habib bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Ramla Al-Azdi, On the authority of Ali: He saw them praying the noon prayer when the sun rose, so he said: Let them not leave it even when the sun was as high as a spear or a spear. Two spears, they prayed, for that is the prayer of the people of repentance."
7887,"(7887) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Zayd, on the authority of Shu`ba, the client of Ibn Abbas, who said: Ibn Abbas used to say Li: Did the fey fall? So if I said yes, he stood up and glorified God."
7888,"(7888) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, who said: Abu Salama would not pray the noon prayer until the sun set. He said: Urwa used to come and pray, then sit."
7889,"(7889) Waki` narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Dathar al-Qattan, on the authority of al-Nu`man bin Nafiz: that Ali went out and saw a people They prayed the noon prayer when the sun rose, and he said: Why should they sacrifice it? God will sacrifice it for them, so do not leave it even if it is on the forehead. Pray, and that is the prayer of the followers of the Prophet."
7890,"(7890) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salih, the client of Umm Hani’, on the authority of Umm Hani’, She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered my house on the day of the conquest of Mecca, and I poured water for him and he washed himself, then prayed. Eight rak'ahs of the Duha prayer, which he did not pray before or after that day. (Tabarani 1003. Ahmad 6/342)"
7891,"(7891) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Shu’abi narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, he said: He did not inform us None of the people said that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the Duha prayer, except Umm Hani’, for she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. He entered my house on the day of the conquest of Mecca. He took a bath, then prayed eight rak’ahs, simplifying the bowing and prostration. I did not see him. They prayed before that day or after it. (Bukhari 1103 and Abu Dawud 1285)"
7892,"(7892) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, who said: I met the people and they were present, or They died, and no one told me that he prayed the Duha prayer except Umm Hani’, for she told me that he prayed eight rak’ahs."
7893,"(7893) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Murra, the client of Umm Hani’. Ibn Abi Talib, on the authority of Umm Hani: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed eight rak’ahs of Dhuha. (Tirmidhi 1579. Ahmad 6/343)"
7894,"(7894) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Ibn Rumaitha, on the authority of his grandmother, she said: I entered upon Aisha. She prayed eight rak'ahs during the forenoon prayer."
7895,"(7895) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id bin Murjaniya, he said: I sat Behind Saad bin Malik, who was reciting the Duha prayer, he prayed eight rak’ahs, I count them, and he did not sit in them until he sat in the last of them. He recited the tashahhud, then saluted and departed."
7896,"(7896) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Tamimah Ibn Diyim: She saw Aisha praying six days of noon prayer. Rakat"
7897,"(7897) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Hakim, on the authority of his grandmother, Ramitha, who said: I entered Aisha's house where she was alone, and I saw her praying eight rak'ahs of the noon prayer."
7898,"(7898) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Umm Salamah: She used to pray the noon prayer, eight. She prayed four rak'ahs while she was sitting, and she was told: Aisha is praying four, and she said: Aisha is a young woman."
7899,"(7899) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah: That when he came to Egypt He prayed four Dhuha prayers."
7900,"(7900) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Hakim bin Hakim, on the authority of Ali bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: I went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to Hurr Banu Muawiyah, and he performed the noon prayer, eight rak’ahs long. Here it is"
7901,"(7901) Ibn Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: His companion, may God bless him and grant him peace, advised me May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, with the two rak’ahs of the forenoon prayer."
7902,"(7902) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ubaid Allah bin Abdul Rahman bin Mawhib narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka`b al-Qurazi, who said : Whoever recites in the Subhāḥ al-Dhuḥah “Say: Allah is One” ten times, a house will be built for him in Paradise."
7903,"(7903) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abu Dhar, it was said to Sufyan: on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes. He said: When one of you stands for prayer, he should not wipe the pebbles. (Abu Dawud 942. Ahmad 5/150)"
7904,"(7904) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir: He used to hate wiping pebbles"
7905,"(7905) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn al-Hakam, on the authority of Shurahbil Abi Saad, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, he said: I do not like that I have red camels, and I have wiped the pebbles from the place of my forehead, unless it overpowers me, so I wipe it clean."
7906,"(7906) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Zaid bin Al-Khattab: He prayed next to Omar, so he wiped the pebbles and held it with his hand."
7907,"(7907) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Atiyya, on the authority of Abu Salih, He said: When you prostrate, do not wipe the pebbles, for every pebble loves to be prostrated on."
7908,"(7908) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Issa bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about certain things, and I even asked him about wiping pebbles, and he said: Pass it once, otherwise leave it. (Abdul Razzaq 2406. Tayalisi 470)"
7909,"(7909) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, on the authority of a sheikh called Hilal, on the authority of Hudhayfă, who said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about everything, even about wiping the pebble, and he said: One, or leave it. (Ahmed 385)"
7910,"(7910) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hisham al-Dastawai narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah Ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Mu’aqib, said: It was mentioned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he wiped the gravel, and he said: If you must do it, you must do it. So one (Bukhari 1207, Abu Dawud 943)"
7911,"(7911) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Shurahbil Abi Saad, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about wiping the pebbles during prayer, and he said: One, and if you refrain from it, it is better for you than... A hundred camels, all of them black. (Ahmad 3/300, Ahmad 328)"
7912,"(7912) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Talha ibn Rukanani, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Ayyash ibn Abu Rabi’a, he said: Abu Dharr passed by me while I was praying. He said: The earth cannot be wiped except once."
7913,"(7913) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Aswad, who said: Abdullah used to make concessions in One wipe for gravel."
7914,"(7914) Ali bin Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of his uncle, he said: I saw Ibn Masoud was leveling the pebbles with his hand while praying, beating them with his hand, then prostrating."
7915,"(7915) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw Abdullah bin Masoud beating the pebbles with his hand, then prostrating."
7916,"(7916) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: He used to permit pebbles to be leveled in Praying once, he said: And if he does not do that, then he is more beloved to me."
7917,"(7917) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja`far, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Ibn Umar was one of those who leveled pebbles. With his feet while standing in prayer."
7918,"(7918) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Malik bin Anas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far al-Qari, the client of Ibn Ayyash, who said: I saw Ibn Umar wiping the pebbles lightly while praying."
7919,"(7919) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, he said: I saw Ibn Umar leveling the pebbles. With his feet during prayer."
7920,"(7920) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Hudhayfah said: Thus, one, or leave, and wipe. In his hand is the earth. Abu Asama said: It means leveling pebbles or something in the place of prostration."
7921,"(7921) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, who said: He used to make a concession in wiping pebbles once."
7922,"(7922) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Ibrahim: He did not see any harm. By leveling the stones once."
7923,"(7923) Abdul-Wahhab bin Ata’ told us, on the authority of Al-Aghar bin Yahya, who said: I saw Al-Hasan placing pebbles where he prostrated. And he was in prayer."
7924,"(7924) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Imran bin Zayd bin Nashit narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi` Abi Dawud, he said: I went out with Ibn Abbas from the mosque, so I took off my socks, and he heard the falling of a pebble, so Ibn Abbas said: Return it, or else I will dispute with you on the Day of Resurrection."
7925,"(7925) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, or On the authority of Kaab, he said: When a pebble is taken out of the mosque, it calls to its owner. (Abu Dawud 460)"
7926,"(7926) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Malik bin Mughul narrated to us, on the authority of Zubaid bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: It is not a hadith. With an updated hadith: If the pebbles are taken out of the mosque, she should shout or say “Tasbih.”"
7927,"(7927) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I asked Hammad about the pebbles he takes out of the mosque with them? He said: Reject them. She asked the arbiter, and he said: Squeeze them until you return, for I heard that they were screaming."
7928,"(7928) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud Abi Al-Haytham, who said: I asked Ibn Sirin about a man who says to his servant, or To his servant: If she finds a pebble in her socks, bring them back to the mosque."
7929,"(7929) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: The pebble curses and curses. Who takes her out of the mosque?"
7930,"(7930) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Muthanna bin Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar, who said: If the pebble is taken out of the mosque, it will shout until it is returned to its place."
7931,"(7931) Asbat told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The pebble is valid if it is taken out of the mosque."
7932,"(7932) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas He said: If you are praying, do not move the pebble."
7933,"(7933) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Abi Hashim, on the authority of Muslim ibn Abi Maryam, who said: Ibn Umar saw A man was turning over pebbles during prayer, and he said: Do not turn over pebbles during prayer, for it is from Satan."
7934,"(7934) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Talha, who said: Turning pebbles is harmful to the kingdom."
7935,"(7935) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ali ibn al-Aqmar, who said: I prayed next to Masruq, then I touched the gravel and it hit. With my hands"
7936,"(7936) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Ziyad bin Fayyad, who said: I prayed next to Abu Iyad and touched the pebbles. So he struck my hand, and when he finished his prayer, he said: A strong word will be said about this."
7937,"(7937) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: When you pray, do not mess with pebbles."
7938,"(7938) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Dinarmuli Atiya, who said: I prayed next to Qays bin Servants, so I took a stick and raised it to my mouth, and he struck my chin. When he prayed, I said to him, “What made you worry?” I liked it, and he said: It used to be said: Whoever tampers with anything in his prayer will have his share of his prayer."
7939,"(7939) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan: He hated for a man to tamper with anything. In his prayers"
7940,"(7940) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman, who said: I prayed next to a man from among the companions of Abdullah, so he touched the pebbles, and when he prayed, he said: Abdullah said: None of you will ask his Lord for anything good while it is in His hand. The stone"
7941,"(7941) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim: He hated tampering with prayer."
7942,"(7942) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Ziyad al-Harithi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying with them on, and he left with them on, meaning his sandals."
7943,"(7943) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Hussein al-Mukhtab, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray barefoot and wearing shoes. (Abu Dawud 653. Ahmad 2/174)"
7944,"(7944) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Shu’abi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Salim, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aws, on the authority of his grandfather: that the Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace. He prayed in his sandals. (Taalisi 1111. Ahmad 4/8)"
7945,"(7945) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Salim, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aws, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. (Ibn Majah 1037)"
7946,"(7946) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of the one who heard Amr bin Harith: that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace And he prayed peace in his shoes. (Nasa’i 9805. Ahmad 4/307)"
7947,"(7947) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin al-Mughirah, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal al-Adawi, on the authority of someone who heard the Bedouin say: : I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying in two sandals made of cows. (Ahmed 6)"
7948,"(7948) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I asked Ata’ whether a man should pray in his shoes? He said: Yes, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed in his sandals."
7949,"(7949) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla: That the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace, may God bless him and grant him peace."
7950,"(7950) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Shu’abi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, who said: The Messenger of God prayed. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was wearing his sandals, and the people prayed in their sandals, so he took them off and they took them off. When he prayed, he said: Whoever wishes may pray. In his sandals, let him pray, and whoever wants to take them off, let him take them off."
7951,"(7951) Ubaid bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Muslima, who said: I asked Anas: Should a man pray in his shoes? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed in his sandals. (Bukhari 3861, Muslim 60)"
7952,"(7952) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took off his sandals and... During prayer, the people took off their shoes, then put them on, and no one was seen taking them off after that."
7953,"(7953) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: Abdullah used to pray in his sandals."
7954,"(7954) Abdi and Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Hakim, who said: I saw Abu Ja’far and Ali bin Hussein. They pray in their shoes."
7955,"(7955) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: I told Shurayh: Should I pray in my shoes? He did not hate it."
7956,"(7956) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Abi Khaled told us, he said: I saw the black man praying in his sandals, and I saw Abu Amr Al-Shaybani beats people if they take off their shoes during prayer."
7957,"(7957) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ziyad bin Fayyad, on the authority of a sheikh of theirs: that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He prayed the salaam in his shoes."
7958,"(7958) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, who said: I saw Ibrahim al-Taymimi leading his people. May God bless him."
7959,"(7959) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father: He used to pray in his shoes."
7960,"(7960) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, he said: Omar used to be strict with people in taking off their shoes during prayer."
7961,"(7961) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Zaid, Salama’s client, who said: I saw Salama praying in his sandals."
7962,"(7962) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham, that he used to pray in his shoes."
7963,"(7963) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, he said: I saw Ibn Abbas praying in his sandals."
7964,"(7964) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, who said: Abraham used to dislike taking off his shoes during prayer. And he says: I wish that a needy person came to the mosque and took their shoes."
7965,"(7965) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of his father: He used to pray in his shoes."
7966,"(7966) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Iyas al-Hanafi, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw Othman prays in his sandals."
7967,"(7967) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Omar, who said: I saw Al-Qasim and Salim praying in their sandals."
7968,"(7968) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Miqdam, he said: I saw Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, Ata bin Yassar, Salim, and Al-Qasim. They pray in their shoes."
7969,"(7969) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman bin Khudair narrated to us, saying: I saw a mujahid, a giving man, and a peacock praying in Their slippers"
7970,"(7970) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Uqba bin Abi Salih narrated to us, saying: I was with Abraham and he was taking off his shoes. When the muezzin said the call to prayer, he put on their clothes."
7971,"(7971) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim bin Ismail bin Mujja’ bin Jariyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ya’qub bin Mujja’, who said: The first person to pray in his shoes was Awaim bin Sa`idah."
7972,"(7972) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Imran bin Hudayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Majliz, that he used to pray in Her shoes"
7973,"(7973) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far: He used to take off his shoes, so when He stood up for prayer wearing his clothes."
7974,"(7974) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Abu Naama, on the authority of Abu Nadrah, on the authority of my father Saeed Al-Khudri: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed and took off his sandals, and the people took off theirs. When he left, he said: Why? Did you take off your shoes? They said: O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, we saw you removed, so we removed. He said: Gabriel came to me and told me that There is evil in them, so when one of you comes to the mosque, he should turn his shoes over and look into them; if he sees in them there is evil. Let him wipe it with the ground and pray over it. (Ahmad 3/20 Darami 1378)"
7975,"(7975) Waki’ told us, he said: Zayd bin Ibrahim al-Tustari told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Take care of your shoes. If one of you sees any harm in them, let him remove them, otherwise let him pray in them."
7976,"(7976) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, he said: Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Alqamiya, he said, and he did not hear it. From him, on the authority of Abdullah: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed in his shoes. (Tayalisi 3951, Ahmad 1/461)"
7977,"(7977) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ghaylan bin Abdullah, the client of Banu Makhzum, who said: I saw Ibn Umar wearing shoes. This is the Sabbath day, so when he prays, he takes them off."
7978,"(7978) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, that Ibn Masoud came to Abu Musa In his house, the time for prayer came, so Abu Musa said to Abdullah: Come forward, and Abdullah said: You have more right, so Abu Musa came forward and he took off. He put on his shoes, and he said to him: Are you Abdullah in the Holy Valley? (Abdul Razzaq 1507)"
7979,"(7979) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abbad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Sa'ib: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed on the day of the conquest of Mecca, and he placed his sandals on his left side. (Abu Dawud 648. Ahmad 3/411)"
7980,"(7980) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of his father, he said: I told my father Huraira: What should I do with my shoes when I pray? He said: Place them between your feet, and do not harm a Muslim with them."
7981,"(7981) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Ubaidah narrated to us, saying: I heard Nafi’ bin Jubayr saying: A man puts on his sandals. Whoever begins prayer with an invocation."
7982,"(7982) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Hakim al-Hadrami, who said: I saw Ibn Umar taking off He put on his shoes and put them behind him."
7983,"(7983) Shababih narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When one of you prays, let him place his sandals between his feet. (Abu Dawud 1455. Ibn Hibban 2182)"
7984,"(7984) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Abu Na’am al-Saadi told us, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Saeed said: While the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying, he took off his sandals and placed them on his left side. (Abu Dawud 650. Ahmad 3/92)"
7985,"(7985) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Abu Usama narrated to us, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Marthad, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Buraida, on the authority of His father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led us in prayer, and a man said: Who called for the red camel? The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No, but the mosques were built for what they were built for. (Muslim 81. Ahmad 5/361)"
7986,"(7986) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of his father, he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab heard A man raised his voice in the mosque and said: Do you know where you are?"
7987,"(7987) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amri told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar: Omar forbade commotion in the mosque, He said: In this mosque of ours, voices are not raised."
7988,"(7988) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard a man chanting He got lost in the mosque and said: No, I found it."
7989,"(7989) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, or Asim, who said: I do not know him except, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Ibn Masoud heard a man seeking for a lost person in the mosque, so he got up to him and reached him."
7990,"(7990) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Amr bin Shu’aib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade buying and selling in the mosque, and the pursuit of lost people. (Tirmidhi 322, Ahmad 2/179)"
7991,"(7991) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Musa ibn Ubaidah, on the authority of Amr ibn Abi Amr, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, He said: A man entered the mosque seeking something lost, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard his voice and said: No, I found it."
7992,"(7992) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Ubaid Allah bin Umar narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, that Abdullah informed him: That Omar was He went out to pray and called out in the mosque, saying: Beware of confusion."
7993,"(7993) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn al-Munkadir, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard a man seeking a lost person. The mosque, and he said: O seeker, someone else is the one who finds it."
7994,"(7994) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Say, “No, I found it.”"
7995,"(7995) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: When the time for prayer comes and the evening meal is served, start with the evening meal. (Bukhari 671, Muslim 65)"
7996,"(7996) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If he attends the dinner The prayer was established, so they began with the evening meal. (Bukhari 672 and Tirmidhi 353)"
7997,"(7997) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: Abdullah bin Rafi’ narrated to us, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: If dinner is prepared and the prayer is ready, start with dinner. (Ahmad 6/291, Abu Ali 6957)"
7998,"(7998) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ubaid Allah ibn Umar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: If dinner is served for one of you and the prayer is performed, start with the dinner and do not rush until it is finished.
 Nafi’ said: Ibn Umar used to put food for him and then the prayer would be performed, but he would not come to it until he had finished, and he would only listen to the people reciting it. Imam (Bukhari 673 and Abu Dawud 3751)"
7999,"(7999) Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Ayoub bin Utba, on the authority of Iyas bin Salamah, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: When the time for prayer and dinner comes, start with dinner. (Ahmad 4/49. Tabarani 6250)"
8000,"(8000) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: When the time for dinner and prayer comes, start with dinner. (Ahmad 3/238)"
8001,"(8001) Hushaym told us, saying: Humayd told us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, similar to that, but the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not mention it. May God bless him and grant him peace."
8002,"(8002) Abdul-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If The dinner has been prepared and the prayer has been established, so they begin with the dinner."
8003,"(8003) Waki’ told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: We were on food for ourselves. I attended the prayer and Abu Talha imprisoned me."
8004,"(8004) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of Ibn Abi al-Malih, on the authority of his father, who said: We were with Abu Bakr had gone out for the Maghrib prayer and the muezzin called the call to prayer. You were presented with a bowl containing porridge and meat, so he said: Sit. So eat, for the food was prepared to be eaten, so he ate, then called for water, washed the tips of his fingers, rinsed his mouth, and prayed."
8005,"(8005) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Abu Asim, on the authority of Ali bin Ubaid Allah, who said: Yasar bin Numayr invited us to a meal. At sunset, he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab used to say: Start with your food, then devote yourselves to your prayers."
8006,"(8006) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Asim, on the authority of Yasar bin Numayr, who said: Omar said: When the dinner is served The prayer was established, so they began with the evening meal."
8007,"(8007) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Qanan bin Abdullah Al-Nahmi, on the authority of their sheikhs, who said: We were at Ali and he prepared to break the fast in Ramadan, and Ali said to us: Break your fast, for it is better for your prayers."
8008,"(8008) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq: that Al-Hasan bin Ali used to say the evening prayer before the prayer to relieve the soul. Blame"
8009,"(8009) They narrated?? Waki`, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Uthman al-Thaqafi, on the authority of a man called Ziyad, who said: We were with Ibn Abbas and he had some barbecue for him. In the oven and the time for prayer came, we said to him, and he said: No, until we eat, it will not be presented to us in our prayer."
8010,"(8010) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, who said: When your dinner is brought and the prayer is called So start with dinner, then prayer."
8011,"(8011) Shababah narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, who said: I came from Iraq, and dinner was approached. Abu Talha and with him were some of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, willing, and he said to him: Come and eat. I said: Until I pray. He said: You have followed the morals of the people of Iraq. Come and eat."
8012,"(8012) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraida, he said: Abdullah bin Amr said: What I don't care if they were stuck on one side of my dress, or they were disputing with me about my prayer."
8013,"(8013) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: Omar said: Do not treat unclean people in prayer and defecate. And urine."
8014,"(8014) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Hurra, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Omar, similar to that."
8015,"(8015) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: None of you should pray. He removes the cesspool of defecation and urination."
8016,"(8016) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Kathir, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: I don’t care whether I defend him, or I pray. And it is in the side of my garment."
